(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const q=(prompt,answer,d1,d2,explain,sense=1,type='meaning')=>({prompt,answer,d1,d2,explain,sense,type});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:'Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/'+w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')});
const P=(w,origin,c,m,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(c)?c:[c],mistakes:[m],quiz:qs.map((x,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+x.sense,type:'辨义与用法',prompt:x.prompt,options:[x.answer,x.d1,x.d2],answer:x.answer,explain:x.explain,errorType:x.type}))});
P('slightly','Slightly is formed from slight and -ly; it means by a small amount or, of a person’s build, in a small and thin way.',[C('slightly.s1','稍微；略微','The soup was slightly too salty, so the cook added a little water before serving it.','汤稍微有点咸，所以厨师在上桌前加了少许水。','The soup was slightly too salty / so the cook added / a little water.','slightly.s1 指程度、数量或大小有一点但不多。','加水只略微改变了味道。'),C('slightly.s2','（身材）瘦小地','The slightly built runner carried a compact pack and moved easily along the narrow trail.','这名身材瘦小的跑者背着轻便背包，轻松地沿窄道前进。','The slightly built runner carried a compact pack / and moved easily / along the trail.','slightly.s2 用于身材时指体形小而瘦。','短语 slightly built 描述瘦小体格。')],M('The soup was slightly too salty, meaning it was unbearably salty and impossible to eat.','The soup was slightly too salty, meaning it was only a little too salty.','slightly 表示程度不大，不是极端严重。','meaning'),[q('How salty was the soup?','a little too salty','so salty it could not be eaten','not salty at all','这汤只是稍微有点咸。',1,'context'),q('How was the runner described?','small and thin in build','very tall and broad','unwilling to walk','跑者体形瘦小。',2,'context'),q('What does slightly mean about the soup?','by a small amount or degree','to an extreme degree','with a long delay','汤句中的 slightly 指程度只有一点。',1,'meaning'),q('What does slightly built mean?','small and thin in build','strong and heavily muscled','poorly built by a careless worker','slightly built 描述身材小而瘦。',2,'meaning')]);
P('slim','Slim has uncertain Germanic roots; it can mean attractively thin, very small/unlikely as a chance, or try to become thinner through diet and exercise.',[C('slim.s1','苗条的；纤细的','The slim dancer chose a light costume that let her move freely across the stage.','这名苗条的舞者选了一套轻便服装，方便她在舞台上自由移动。','The slim dancer chose a light costume / that let her move / freely across the stage.','slim.s1 指纤细，常含体形匀称、好看的意味。','舞者身材纤细且行动自如。'),C('slim.s2','微小的；机会不大的','There is only a slim chance the late ferry will arrive before the storm closes the harbor.','晚班渡船在风暴封港前抵达的机会很小。','There is only a slim chance / the ferry will arrive / before the storm closes the harbor.','slim.s2 指成功可能性或数量非常小。','风暴将至，按时到达的概率很低。'),C('slim.s3','减肥；变苗条','After her doctor recommended more activity, Rosa began to slim by walking daily and adjusting her meals.','医生建议增加活动量后，罗莎开始每天散步并调整饮食以减重。','Rosa began to slim / by walking daily / and adjusting her meals.','slim.s3 作动词，指通过饮食和运动变瘦。','规律散步和调整饮食帮助减重。')],M('The ferry had a slim chance of arriving, which meant its arrival was virtually guaranteed.','The ferry had a slim chance of arriving, so success was unlikely.','slim chance 表示概率小，不是几乎必然。','meaning'),[q('What did the slim dancer choose?','a light costume for easy movement','a heavy coat for cold water','a large shipload of wool','苗条的舞者选择了轻便服装。',1,'context'),q('How likely was the ferry to arrive before the storm?','unlikely; it had only a small chance','certain; it was guaranteed','impossible because it had sunk','渡船按时抵达的机会很小。',2,'context'),q('What did Rosa do to slim?','walked daily and adjusted her meals','stopped moving and ate more','boarded a ferry during a storm','罗莎通过日常散步和调整饮食来减重。',3,'context'),q('What does slim mean in “a slim chance”?','very small and unlikely','thin in an attractive physical way','an effort to lose weight','slim chance 指可能性很小。',2,'meaning')]);
P('slime','Slime is recorded in Middle English for a sticky substance; it can mean mucus covering some small creatures or soft wet mud.',[C('slime.s1','体表黏液','The snail left a trail of slime across the leaf as it moved toward the damp wall.','蜗牛爬向潮湿的墙时，在叶片上留下一道黏液痕迹。','The snail left slime across the leaf / as it moved / toward the damp wall.','slime.s1 指覆盖某些小动物皮肤的黏滑液体。','蜗牛移动后留下黏液。'),C('slime.s2','黏滑的污泥','Rain turned the unpaved path into slime, and several hikers had to walk slowly to avoid slipping.','雨水把未铺装的小路变成了黏滑泥地，几名徒步者只好慢慢走以免滑倒。','Rain turned the path into slime / so hikers walked slowly / to avoid slipping.','slime.s2 指使地面又湿又滑又脏的软泥。','雨后小路变成湿滑泥地。')],M('The snail left a trail of slime even though its path remained completely dry and clean.','The snail left a trail of sticky mucus as it crawled.','干燥洁净的表面与黏液痕迹不符。','meaning'),[q('What left a trail of slime on the leaf?','the snail','the ferry','a wooden shelf','蜗牛在叶片上留下黏液痕迹。',1,'context'),q('What did rain do to the unpaved path?','turned it into soft slippery mud','polished it into a dry stone road','covered it with a wool shawl','雨水把未铺路面变成了黏滑泥地。',2,'context'),q('What is slime in the snail example?','a slippery liquid covering an animal’s skin','a small piece of paper','a ship’s mast','蜗牛句中的 slime 指体表黏液。',1,'meaning'),q('What does slime mean in the muddy path example?','soft wet mud that makes a surface slippery','clear dry pavement','a thin opening in fabric','泥路句中的 slime 指黏滑污泥。',2,'meaning')]);
P('slimy','Slimy is formed from slime and -y; it means wet, sticky, and slippery like mucus or algae.',C('slimy.s1','黏滑的','The slimy stones near the waterfall were difficult to grip, so the climbers used a handrail.','瀑布旁黏滑的石头很难抓牢，因此攀爬者使用了扶手。','The slimy stones were hard to grip / so the climbers / used a handrail.','slimy.s1 指湿黏且容易滑动的。','石头表面湿滑，难以抓握。'),M('The slimy stones were dry and rough, so every climber held them securely without slipping.','The slimy stones were wet and slippery, so the climbers used a handrail.','干燥粗糙而牢固的石头不符合 slimy。','meaning'),[q('Where were the slimy stones?','near the waterfall','inside the dry classroom','on the ferry’s deck','黏滑的石头在瀑布附近。',1,'context'),q('Why did climbers use a handrail?','the stones were difficult to grip','the stones were dry and rough','the path was a flat carpet','因为石头黏滑难抓，攀爬者使用扶手。',1,'context'),q('What does slimy mean?','wet, sticky, and slippery','dry, rough, and easy to hold','very thin and transparent','slimy 指湿黏、滑溜的。',1,'meaning'),q('Which surface is slimy?','wet algae-coated rocks that slip under a hand','dry rough stone with firm grip','a polished wooden floor with no moisture','沾有湿藻、抓上去会滑的石头是 slimy。',1,'context')]);
P('slip','Slip comes from Old English slīpan (“slide”); it can mean lose footing, put something quickly or leave unnoticed, a small mistake, or a paper note/undergarment.',[C('slip.s1','滑；滑倒','I slipped on the wet tile near the entrance but caught the railing before falling.','我在入口附近的湿瓷砖上滑了一下，但抓住扶手没有摔倒。','I slipped on the wet tile / but caught / the railing.','slip.s1 指意外滑动并失去脚下平衡或抓握。','湿瓷砖使人打滑。'),C('slip.s2','迅速塞入；悄悄走','She slipped the spare key into her pocket and slipped out before the guests noticed.','她把备用钥匙迅速塞进口袋，趁客人没注意悄悄离开。','She slipped the key into her pocket / and slipped out / unnoticed.','slip.s2 指迅速放入某处或不被注意地离开。','两个动词用法分别表示塞入和溜走。'),C('slip.s3','小差错；口误','A small slip in the printed schedule listed the meeting at 3 p.m. instead of 2 p.m.','印刷日程里的一个小差错把会议时间写成下午三点，而不是两点。','A small slip in the schedule / listed the meeting / at the wrong time.','slip.s3 指无心犯下的小错误，尤其是口误或笔误。','时间表出现小笔误。'),C('slip.s4','纸条；衬裙','The clerk handed me a claim slip, and the bride wore a light slip beneath her dress.','职员递给我一张取货凭条，而新娘在礼服内穿了一件轻薄衬裙。','The clerk handed me a claim slip / while the bride wore / a slip under her dress.','slip.s4 可指小纸条，也可指穿在裙子里面的轻薄衬裙。','同一义项列出纸条和内衣用法。')],M('I slipped on the wet tile because it was dry and rough and gave my shoes a firm grip.','I slipped on the wet tile because its damp surface was slippery.','湿滑表面会让人失去平衡，干燥粗糙表面不会。','meaning'),[q('What helped the speaker avoid falling?','the railing','a claim slip','the wet tile','说话者抓住扶手后没有摔倒。',1,'context'),q('What did she put into her pocket?','the spare key','the printed schedule','a wet tile','她把备用钥匙塞进口袋。',2,'context'),q('What time error appeared on the schedule?','3 p.m. instead of 2 p.m.','2 p.m. instead of 3 p.m.','the meeting was canceled','日程把下午两点误写成三点。',3,'context'),q('What is a claim slip?','a small piece of paper','a wet surface','a garment worn as an outer coat','claim slip 指一张小纸条或凭条。',4,'meaning')]);
P('slipper','Slipper combines slip and -er; it means a light house shoe with an open back that the foot slides into.',C('slipper.s1','拖鞋；室内便鞋','She left her slippers beside the bed and walked barefoot across the carpet.','她把拖鞋放在床边，赤脚走过地毯。','She left her slippers / beside the bed / and walked across the carpet.','slipper.s1 指后跟敞开、脚可直接滑入的轻便室内鞋。','拖鞋放在床边供室内穿。'),M('She put on a slipper by lacing it tightly around her ankle like a tall hiking boot.','She slid her foot into a light open-backed house shoe.','拖鞋后跟敞开，不像登山靴那样系紧脚踝。','meaning'),[q('Where did she leave her slippers?','beside the bed','on the wet tile outside','in the ferry cabin','她把拖鞋放在床边。',1,'context'),q('How did she walk across the carpet?','barefoot','in a sloping boot','on a slipper tied around her wrist','她赤脚走过地毯。',1,'context'),q('What is a slipper?','a light house shoe with an open back','a tall lace-up hiking boot','a metal horse shoe','slipper 指后跟敞开的轻便室内鞋。',1,'meaning'),q('Which footwear is a slipper?','a soft house shoe the foot slides into','a rigid boot tied to the ankle','a blade cover for a knife','脚可直接滑入的软质室内鞋是 slipper。',1,'context')]);
P('slippery','Slippery comes from slip and -ery; it can mean hard to hold/walk on, untrustworthy, or a situation that is difficult and may worsen.',[C('slippery.s1','滑的；光滑易滑的','The icy steps were slippery, so the caretaker spread sand over them before opening the building.','台阶结冰后很滑，因此管理员在开放建筑前撒了沙子。','The icy steps were slippery / so the caretaker / spread sand.','slippery.s1 指表面湿滑、难以握住或行走的。','沙子增加冰面摩擦。'),C('slippery.s2','狡猾的；靠不住的','The slippery dealer changed his story whenever investigators asked where the missing funds had gone.','调查人员每次询问失踪资金去向时，这名狡猾的商人都会改口。','The slippery dealer changed his story / whenever investigators / asked about the funds.','slippery.s2 形容人时指狡猾、不可信。','他遇到追问便改口。'),C('slippery.s3','棘手的；易出问题的','The committee faced a slippery situation because one small delay could cause several linked deadlines to be missed.','委员会面临棘手局面，因为一次小延误就可能导致好几个相关期限错过。','The committee faced a slippery situation / because one delay / could disrupt linked deadlines.','slippery.s3 可形容难处理且可能恶化的处境。','小延误可能造成连锁问题。')],M('The slippery dealer was trustworthy because he gave investigators the same accurate account every time.','The slippery dealer was untrustworthy because he repeatedly changed his story.','始终如实陈述不符合狡猾、不可靠的含义。','meaning'),[q('Why did the caretaker spread sand?','the icy steps were slippery','the steps were dry and rough','the building had no entrance','冰台阶很滑，管理员撒沙防滑。',1,'context'),q('What did the dealer do when asked about the missing funds?','changed his story','provided the same account each time','closed the harbor','商人被问及资金时反复改口。',2,'context'),q('What could one delay do in the committee’s slippery situation?','cause several linked deadlines to be missed','make the ice steps rough','restore every deadline automatically','一次延误可能导致多个相关期限错过。',3,'context'),q('What does slippery mean about the dealer?','clever but difficult to trust','easy to hold securely','calm and reliable','slippery 描述人时指狡猾、不可信。',2,'meaning')]);
P('slipup','Slipup combines slip and up; it means a careless error rather than a major fault in a plan.',C('slipup.s1','差错；疏忽','A slipup in the mailing list sent two invitations to the same address.','邮寄名单中的一个疏忽导致两张邀请函寄到了同一地址。','A slipup in the mailing list / sent two invitations / to one address.','slipup.s1 指因粗心造成的小错误，而非计划本身的重大缺陷。','重复寄送源于名单里的小疏忽。'),M('The duplicate invitations were a slipup caused by a carefully tested plan with no careless error.','The duplicate invitations resulted from a careless mistake in the mailing list.','名单疏忽意味着存在小差错。','meaning'),[q('What did the mailing-list slipup cause?','two invitations to go to one address','the invitations to be canceled','the harbor to close','名单疏忽让两张邀请函寄到了同一地址。',1,'context'),q('What kind of error was it?','a careless small mistake','a major failure in the whole plan','a planned change to the address','这是名单中的一个小疏忽。',1,'context'),q('What is a slipup?','an error caused by carelessness','a deliberate improvement to a plan','a narrow opening in a wall','slipup 指粗心造成的差错。',1,'meaning'),q('Which event is a slipup?','accidentally entering the same address twice','deliberately mailing one invitation to each guest','canceling an event because the venue is unsafe','误把同一地址输入两次是 slipup。',1,'context')]);
P('slit','Slit is recorded in English from Old English; it can mean a narrow opening, a narrow viewing/firing opening in a wall, or make such a long narrow cut.',[C('slit.s1','窄缝；细长开口','A narrow slit in the envelope let the clerk see only the corner of the letter inside.','信封上的细长窄缝只让职员看到里面信纸的一角。','A narrow slit in the envelope / let the clerk see / one corner of the letter.','slit.s1 指布、纸或木头表面上的细长开口。','信封上有细长开口。'),C('slit.s2','（墙上的）窥视狭孔；枪眼','The old fortress had a slit in the stone wall through which a guard could watch the road.','古堡石墙上有一个狭孔，守卫可以从那里观察道路。','The fortress had a slit in the wall / through which a guard / watched the road.','slit.s2 指墙上用于观察或射击的狭窄开口。','守卫从墙孔观察道路。'),C('slit.s3','切开；划出狭缝','The tailor slit the fabric along the marked line so it would fit over the chair back.','裁缝沿标记线把布料划开一道缝，使它能套在椅背上。','The tailor slit the fabric / along the marked line / to fit the chair back.','slit.s3 作动词指在某物上切出细长开口。','布料沿线被裁开。')],M('The tailor slit the fabric by leaving it completely uncut and without any opening.','The tailor cut a long narrow opening in the fabric along the marked line.','未切开且没有开口，与 slit 相反。','meaning'),[q('What could the clerk see through the envelope slit?','one corner of the letter','the entire letter clearly','the road outside the fortress','信封窄缝只让职员看见信纸一角。',1,'context'),q('What could a fortress guard do through the wall slit?','watch the road','mail an invitation','repair a slippery stair','守卫可以从墙上的狭孔观察道路。',2,'context'),q('What did the tailor slit?','the fabric','the stone road','the envelope clerk','裁缝沿线把布料划开。',3,'context'),q('What does slit mean as a noun?','a long narrow opening','a large round room','a careless mistake','slit 名词指细长的开口。',1,'meaning')]);
P('slither','Slither is probably imitative in origin, suggesting a sliding movement; it means slide or glide along with a twisting motion.',C('slither.s1','蜿蜒滑行','The snake slithered beneath the fallen log and disappeared into the grass.','蛇蜿蜒滑过倒下的木头，消失在草丛里。','The snake slithered beneath the log / and disappeared / into the grass.','slither.s1 指带着扭动动作贴着表面滑行。','蛇贴地蜿蜒移动。'),M('The snake slithered beneath the log by flying straight above it without touching the ground.','The snake slid along the ground with a twisting motion beneath the log.','飞在空中没有贴地滑动。','meaning'),[q('Where did the snake slither?','beneath the fallen log','across the roof of the shop','inside a shipload of grain','蛇蜿蜒滑到倒木下面。',1,'context'),q('Where did it disappear?','into the grass','into the harbor','inside the envelope','蛇消失在草丛里。',1,'context'),q('What does slither mean?','slide along with a twisting motion','fly upward without touching a surface','walk with short careful steps','slither 指扭动着贴面滑行。',1,'meaning'),q('Which movement is slithering?','a snake twisting as it glides under a log','a bird soaring above a cliff','a runner climbing a ladder','蛇扭动身体滑过木头属于 slither。',1,'context')]);
P('slog','Slog is of uncertain origin; it means keep working or walking despite a task being long and tiring.',C('slog.s1','苦干；跋涉','We slogged through the muddy field for hours to deliver supplies to the isolated farm.','我们在泥泞的田地里艰难跋涉数小时，把物资送到偏远农场。','We slogged through the muddy field / for hours / to deliver supplies.','slog.s1 指在疲劳、困难的条件下持续工作或行走。','长时间泥地跋涉十分辛苦。'),M('We slogged through the field by gliding effortlessly across dry pavement in a few seconds.','We slogged through the muddy field for hours despite the tiring conditions.','轻松几秒穿过干燥地面不是艰苦跋涉。','meaning'),[q('Where did the group slog?','through a muddy field','across a polished shop floor','along a dry indoor corridor','他们在泥泞田地里艰难跋涉。',1,'context'),q('How long did the walk take?','hours','a few seconds','one minute exactly','跋涉持续了数小时。',1,'context'),q('What does slog mean?','keep working or walking despite tiring difficulty','move smoothly and effortlessly','stop after a brief rest','slog 指在困难劳累中持续工作或行走。',1,'meaning'),q('Which task is a slog?','carrying supplies across deep mud for hours','sliding easily down a dry ramp','shopping briefly at a nearby store','在深泥中运送物资数小时是 slog。',1,'context')]);
P('slogan','Slogan comes from Scottish Gaelic sluagh-ghairm (“war cry”); it means a short memorable phrase used in advertising or to state a political aim.',C('slogan.s1','口号；标语','The campaign’s slogan, “Clean rivers, shared future,” appeared on posters along the town’s bridges.','竞选口号“清洁河流，共享未来”出现在镇上各座桥边的海报上。','The campaign’s slogan appeared / on posters / along the town’s bridges.','slogan.s1 指广告或政治宣传中简短、易记的口号。','海报反复展示同一句口号。'),M('The campaign slogan was a twenty-page report with detailed tables and no brief phrase.','The campaign used a short memorable phrase on its posters.','长篇报告不是简短易记的口号。','meaning'),[q('What was the campaign slogan?','“Clean rivers, shared future”','“Bridge inspection at 3 p.m.”','“The ferry sailed at dawn”','竞选口号是“清洁河流，共享未来”。',1,'context'),q('Where did the slogan appear?','on posters along the bridges','only inside a ship’s hold','on a shoelace','口号出现在镇上各座桥边的海报上。',1,'context'),q('What is a slogan?','a short memorable phrase for advertising or a cause','a detailed twenty-page technical report','a schedule listing every worker','slogan 指用于广告或政治目标的简短易记短语。',1,'meaning'),q('Which text is a slogan?','“Save the wetlands, protect our future”','a long contract with legal clauses','a list of delivery addresses','“保护湿地，守护未来”这样的短语是 slogan。',1,'context')]);
P('sloop','Sloop is from Dutch sloep, ultimately of uncertain origin; it means a sailing vessel with one mast, usually carrying a mainsail and headsail.',C('sloop.s1','单桅帆船','The small sloop sailed out of the harbor under one mast as the morning wind filled its two sails.','晨风鼓起两面帆时，这艘小型单桅帆船驶出了港口。','The small sloop sailed out / under one mast / with two sails filled by wind.','sloop.s1 指通常装有主帆和前帆的单桅帆船。','船只有一根桅杆。'),M('The sloop carried five masts and used no sails, relying entirely on a jet engine.','The sloop sailed with a single mast carrying its mainsail and headsail.','多桅且靠喷气发动机航行的船不是 sloop。','meaning'),[q('How many masts did the sloop have?','one','five','none; it used a jet engine','例句中的小帆船有一根桅杆。',1,'context'),q('What filled the sails?','the morning wind','an electric battery','a sheet of rain indoors','晨风鼓起帆面。',1,'context'),q('What is a sloop?','a sailing vessel with one mast','a large passenger ferry with many decks','a workroom where ships are repaired','sloop 指单桅帆船。',1,'meaning'),q('Which vessel is a sloop?','a small boat rigged with one mast and a mainsail','a motor vessel with five masts and no sails','a shipyard crane','一根桅杆并装有主帆的小船是 sloop。',1,'context')]);
P('slop','Slop is from Middle English for muddy or spilled liquid; it can mean soft spilled food/liquid or spill liquid messily.',[C('slop.s1','泔水；残羹剩汁','The farmer poured the kitchen slop into a bucket for the pigs.','农夫把厨房残羹倒进桶里喂猪。','The farmer poured the kitchen slop / into a bucket / for the pigs.','slop.s1 指洒出的液体或喂牲畜的软烂废食。','残羹被收集起来喂猪。'),C('slop.s2','泼洒；溅出','Be careful not to slop coffee over the map while you carry the cup across the table.','端着咖啡穿过桌子时，小心别把咖啡洒到地图上。','Be careful not to slop coffee / over the map / while carrying the cup.','slop.s2 作动词，指让液体不小心洒出容器或凌乱地流出。','端杯时咖啡可能溅出。')],M('He slopped coffee across the map without spilling a drop from the full cup.','He slopped coffee across the map by spilling it messily.','咖啡没有洒出就不会弄到地图上。','meaning'),[q('What did the farmer pour into the bucket?','kitchen slop','a clean new map','a dry shoe','农夫把厨房残羹倒进桶里。',1,'context'),q('What might spill over the map?','coffee','a sheepfold','a slogan','端咖啡时可能把咖啡洒到地图上。',2,'context'),q('What does slop mean in the bucket example?','soft leftover food or spilled liquid','a short advertising phrase','a steep hillside','桶里的 slop 指残羹或软烂废食。',1,'meaning'),q('What does slop mean as a verb?','spill liquid messily','pour carefully without spilling','slide with a twisting motion','slop 作动词指凌乱地泼洒液体。',2,'meaning')]);
P('slope','Slope comes from Middle English as a variant of aslope; it can mean slanted ground, the angle of not being flat, or be inclined.',[C('slope.s1','斜坡；坡地','The cyclists climbed the steep slope toward the lookout above the valley.','骑行者沿陡坡爬向山谷上方的观景台。','The cyclists climbed the steep slope / toward the lookout / above the valley.','slope.s1 指向上或向下倾斜的一片地面或表面。','骑行者沿斜坡攀登。'),C('slope.s2','倾斜；坡度','The engineer measured the slope of the ramp to ensure wheelchairs could use it safely.','工程师测量了坡道的倾斜度，以确保轮椅可以安全通行。','The engineer measured the slope / of the ramp / for wheelchair access.','slope.s2 指表面不平的程度或倾斜角度。','坡道角度影响无障碍通行。'),C('slope.s3','倾斜','The roof slopes toward the gutter so rainwater drains away from the entrance.','屋顶朝排水槽方向倾斜，使雨水远离入口排走。','The roof slopes toward the gutter / so rainwater / drains away from the entrance.','slope.s3 作动词指一端高于另一端而倾斜。','屋顶坡向排水槽。')],M('The roof slopes toward the entrance by remaining perfectly level from end to end.','The roof slopes toward the gutter so rain drains away.','完全水平的屋顶没有倾斜。','meaning'),[q('Where were the cyclists climbing?','up a steep slope toward a lookout','down a flat indoor hallway','through a shop centre','骑行者沿陡坡爬向观景台。',1,'context'),q('Why did the engineer measure the ramp’s slope?','to check safe wheelchair access','to determine the slogan’s length','to count a shipload','工程师测量坡道倾斜度以确保轮椅安全通行。',2,'context'),q('What does the roof do in the final example?','slopes toward the gutter','stays perfectly level','slips into the entrance','屋顶朝排水槽方向倾斜。',3,'context'),q('What is a slope in the ramp example?','the angle or degree to which the ramp is not flat','a small careless error','a liquid spilled from a cup','坡道例句中的 slope 指倾斜角度。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sloping','Sloping is formed from slope and -ing; it describes a surface set at an incline, with one side higher than the other.',C('sloping.s1','倾斜的','They planted grapevines on the sloping hillside where rain could drain away from the roots.','他们把葡萄藤种在倾斜的山坡上，雨水可以从根部排走。','They planted grapevines / on the sloping hillside / where rain drained away.','sloping.s1 指一侧高于另一侧的倾斜表面。','山坡有利于排水。'),M('The vineyard was on sloping ground that was completely flat from top to bottom.','The vineyard was on inclined ground where water could drain downhill.','完全平坦的土地不是 sloping。','meaning'),[q('Where did they plant grapevines?','on the sloping hillside','inside a flat shop','beneath a ferry deck','葡萄藤种在倾斜的山坡上。',1,'context'),q('What happened to rainwater there?','it drained away from the roots','it remained trapped above the vines','it flowed uphill','雨水能从葡萄藤根部排走。',1,'context'),q('What does sloping mean?','set at an incline, with one side higher','level and horizontal','wet and sticky like slime','sloping 指倾斜的。',1,'meaning'),q('Which path is sloping?','a path that descends from a hilltop to a valley','a level corridor with no incline','a vertical slit in a wall','从山顶向山谷下降的小路是 sloping。',1,'context')]);
P('sloppy','Sloppy is formed from slop and -y; it can mean careless or untidy, or wet, soft, and unpleasantly messy.',[C('sloppy.s1','马虎的；不整洁的','The editor returned the sloppy draft because it contained missing citations and several unfinished sentences.','编辑退回了这份马虎的草稿，因为它缺少引文，还有几处句子未写完。','The editor returned the sloppy draft / with missing citations / and unfinished sentences.','sloppy.s1 指做事不认真或外观凌乱的。','草稿存在多处疏漏。'),C('sloppy.s2','泥泞的；稀软的','After the thaw, the path became sloppy mud that clung to everyone’s boots.','解冻后，小路变成稀软泥地，粘在每个人的靴子上。','The path became sloppy mud / after the thaw / and clung to boots.','sloppy.s2 指湿软、凌乱难受的状态。','融雪后泥土稀软。')],M('The sloppy draft was carefully checked, complete, and free of any missing sources or unfinished lines.','The sloppy draft contained missing citations and unfinished sentences.','完整、仔细核实的稿件不符合马虎的描述。','meaning'),[q('Why did the editor return the draft?','it lacked citations and had unfinished sentences','it contained too many verified sources','it was written on a sloping hill','草稿缺引文且有未完成句子。',1,'context'),q('What happened to the path after the thaw?','it became wet, soft mud','it froze into dry rock','it turned into a shop','解冻后的小路变成了稀软泥地。',2,'context'),q('What does sloppy mean about the draft?','careless or untidy','wet and slippery','short and unlikely','草稿句中的 sloppy 指马虎、不整洁。',1,'meaning'),q('What does sloppy mean about the path?','soft, wet, and unpleasantly messy','carefully organized','steep but dry','path 句中的 sloppy 指湿软泥泞。',2,'meaning')]);
P('slot','Slot is of uncertain origin; it can mean a narrow opening, a position/time in a schedule, or put something into an opening/arrange a time.',[C('slot.s1','狭缝；投币口','Insert the card into the slot on the ticket machine and wait for the green light.','把卡插入售票机的狭缝，然后等待绿灯亮起。','Insert the card into the slot / on the ticket machine / and wait.','slot.s1 指细长的开口。','卡片要插入机器开口。'),C('slot.s2','位置；时段','The clinic offered me a morning slot for the vaccination appointment.','诊所给我安排了一个上午时段接种疫苗。','The clinic offered a morning slot / for the vaccination / appointment.','slot.s2 指清单、机器或时间表中的位置或时段。','接种安排在上午时间段。'),C('slot.s3','插入；安排进','The producer slotted the interview between the evening news and the weather report.','制片人把采访安排在晚间新闻和天气预报之间。','The producer slotted the interview / between the news / and the weather report.','slot.s3 作动词，指把东西插入开口或安排进某个时段。','采访被安排在两个节目之间。')],M('The producer slotted the interview between two programs by placing it outside the schedule with no broadcast time.','The producer slotted the interview into the schedule between the two programs.','没有安排在节目表中就不算排入时段。','meaning'),[q('Where should the card go?','into the slot on the ticket machine','onto the clinic’s roof','inside the weather report','卡片要插入售票机的狭缝。',1,'context'),q('What appointment time did the clinic offer?','a morning slot','a midnight slot only','no appointment time at all','诊所给了上午接种时段。',2,'context'),q('Where did the producer slot the interview?','between the evening news and weather report','after the broadcast had ended','inside the ticket machine','采访被安排在晚间新闻和天气预报之间。',3,'context'),q('What does slot mean as a noun in “morning slot”?','a place in a schedule','a narrow opening in a machine','an act of sliding on ice','morning slot 指时间表中的一个时段。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sloth','Sloth comes from Old English slǣwþ (“laziness”); it means laziness or a slow-moving tree-dwelling mammal of Central and South America.',[C('sloth.s1','懒惰；怠惰','The coach blamed sloth, not lack of talent, for the team’s failure to practice between games.','教练认为球队比赛间不练习是出于懒惰，而不是缺乏天赋。','The coach blamed sloth / for the team’s failure / to practice between games.','sloth.s1 指避免工作或努力的习惯。','球队因怠惰而不练习。'),C('sloth.s2','树懒','A sloth moved slowly through the branches while the researchers watched from the forest floor.','研究人员在林地上观察一只树懒缓慢地穿过树枝。','A sloth moved slowly / through the branches / as researchers watched.','sloth.s2 指中美洲和南美洲树栖、行动缓慢的哺乳动物。','树懒在树枝间移动。')],M('The team showed sloth by practicing for hours every day and arriving early for each training session.','The team showed sloth by avoiding practice between games.','勤奋练习与懒惰相反。','meaning'),[q('What did the coach blame for the missed practices?','sloth','a steep slope','a ticket slot','教练认为球队因懒惰而不练习。',1,'context'),q('Where did the sloth move?','through the branches','across the harbor','inside a ticket machine','树懒在树枝间缓慢移动。',2,'context'),q('What does sloth mean in the coach’s comment?','laziness','a small mammal','a work schedule','教练句中的 sloth 指懒惰。',1,'meaning'),q('What is a sloth in the forest example?','a slow-moving mammal that lives in trees','a person who refuses to work','a bird that feeds on a shore','森林句中的 sloth 指树懒这种树栖哺乳动物。',2,'meaning')]);
P('slothful','Slothful is formed from sloth and -ful; it means unwilling to work or make effort, and therefore lazy or slow in action.',C('slothful.s1','懒惰的；怠惰的','The slothful clerk postponed the simple filing task for a week despite having ample time to complete it.','尽管时间充裕，这名懒惰的职员仍把简单的归档工作拖了一周。','The slothful clerk postponed the task / for a week / despite ample time.','slothful.s1 指不愿工作或付出努力、做事拖沓的。','有时间却拖延简单任务。'),M('The slothful clerk completed the filing promptly and volunteered for extra work without being asked.','The slothful clerk delayed the filing despite having time to do it.','主动及时完成任务体现勤奋，不是 slothful。','meaning'),[q('How long did the clerk delay the filing task?','a week','one minute','a year of continuous work','职员把归档工作拖了一周。',1,'context'),q('Did the clerk have enough time?','yes, ample time','no, the deadline had passed before the task arrived','the task took several years','职员有充足时间完成任务。',1,'context'),q('What does slothful mean?','unwilling to work or make effort','quick and careful','very small in size','slothful 指懒惰、不愿付出努力的。',1,'meaning'),q('Which employee is slothful?','one who delays a simple task despite having time','one who finishes early and volunteers for more','one who asks for a clear deadline','有时间却拖延简单工作的员工是 slothful。',1,'context')]);
P('slouch','Slouch is recorded from the late Middle English period for a drooping posture; it names a lazy, bent way of sitting, standing, or walking.',C('slouch.s1','无精打采的姿势；弯腰驼背','Instead of sitting upright at the interview, Leo began to slouch in his chair with his shoulders rounded.','利奥没有在面试时坐直，反而弓着肩膀瘫靠在椅子上。','Leo began to slouch in his chair / with his shoulders / rounded.','slouch.s1 指懒散地弯腰或垂肩坐、站、走的姿势。','圆肩瘫坐体现 slouch。'),M('Leo slouched in the interview by sitting erect, shoulders back, and eyes level throughout.','Leo slouched by sitting with rounded shoulders and a drooping posture.','挺直坐姿与 slouch 所指的弯垂姿势相反。','meaning'),[q('How did Leo sit during the interview?','with rounded shoulders and a drooping posture','upright with his shoulders back','on the floor beside the chair','利奥弓着肩膀瘫靠在椅子上。',1,'context'),q('Which posture is a slouch?','a bent, drooping way of sitting','a straight-backed attentive stance','a quick step down a slope','弯腰垂肩的坐姿是 slouch。',1,'meaning'),q('What did Leo do instead of sitting upright?','he slouched in his chair','he ran out of the room','he adjusted the interview schedule','他在椅子上弓背瘫坐。',1,'context'),q('What does slouch describe here?','a lazy, bent posture','a formal interview question','a sudden business decline','这里的 slouch 指懒散弯垂的姿势。',1,'meaning')]);
P('slouchy','Slouchy is formed from slouch and -y; it describes clothes or posture that hang or sag in an untidy, relaxed way.',C('slouchy.s1','松垮的；懒散的','The slouchy sweater hung loosely from her shoulders, giving the outfit a relaxed rather than formal look.','那件松垮的毛衣从她肩上宽松地垂下来，让整套穿着显得随意而非正式。','The slouchy sweater hung loosely / from her shoulders / and looked relaxed.','slouchy.s1 形容衣服宽松下垂或姿势懒散、不挺拔。','毛衣宽松垂坠，整体风格休闲。'),M('Her slouchy sweater was sharply tailored and fitted closely at every seam.','Her slouchy sweater hung loosely and looked relaxed.','紧身、剪裁利落的衣服不符合 slouchy 的宽松下垂感。','meaning'),[q('How did the sweater fit?','loosely, hanging from her shoulders','tightly at every seam','like a stiff uniform jacket','毛衣宽松地从肩上垂下来。',1,'context'),q('What look did the sweater give the outfit?','relaxed rather than formal','strictly formal and sharply tailored','wet and muddy','穿搭因此显得随意而不正式。',1,'context'),q('What does slouchy mean about clothing?','loose and sagging in an untidy relaxed way','tightly fitted and crisp','made of metal mesh','slouchy 形容宽松下垂、较随意的衣物。',1,'meaning'),q('Which garment is slouchy?','an oversized cardigan drooping from the shoulders','a fitted jacket with crisp seams','a rigid protective helmet','宽大并从肩部垂下的开衫是 slouchy。',1,'context')]);
P('slough','Slough is from Old English slēah, “skin cast by a snake”; as a verb it means to shed skin, tissue, or an unwanted habit.',C('slough.s1','蜕去；抛弃','As the injured snake healed, it began to slough its old skin in one dull, papery layer.','受伤的蛇康复时，开始一层层蜕去暗淡、纸状的旧皮。','The snake began to slough its old skin / in one papery layer / as it healed.','slough.s1 作动词，指脱落或蜕去皮肤、组织，也可比喻抛弃习惯。','蛇康复时蜕去旧皮。'),M('The snake sloughed its old skin by keeping every layer firmly attached as it grew.','The snake sloughed its old skin by shedding the outer layer.','蜕皮意味着旧皮脱落，而非始终附着。','meaning'),[q('What did the snake slough?','its old skin','the branch it was resting on','a paper map','蛇蜕去了旧皮。',1,'context'),q('What was the skin like as it came away?','dull and papery','bright metal and rigid','wet snow','旧皮呈暗淡的纸状。',1,'context'),q('What does slough mean in the sentence?','shed an outer layer of skin','hold an object tightly','sit with rounded shoulders','这里的 slough 指蜕去外层皮肤。',1,'meaning'),q('Which action is to slough a habit?','gradually abandon an unwanted habit','make a habit permanent','hide a habit under clothing','slough a habit 指逐渐抛弃不想要的习惯。',1,'meaning')]);
P('slovenly','Slovenly is based on sloven, a careless or untidy person; it means dirty or careless in appearance or in the way work is done.',C('slovenly.s1','邋遢的；马虎的','The inspector called the workshop slovenly because oil-stained tools were scattered across the floor.','检查员说车间邋遢，因为沾油的工具散落在地板上。','The inspector called the workshop slovenly / because stained tools / littered the floor.','slovenly.s1 指外表或做事方式脏乱、粗心。','工具乱放且沾满油污。'),M('The inspector praised the slovenly workshop because every clean tool was labeled and stored neatly.','The inspector called it slovenly because dirty tools lay scattered on the floor.','工具洁净有序与 slovenly 所指的脏乱相反。','meaning'),[q('Why did the inspector call the workshop slovenly?','oil-stained tools were scattered on the floor','all tools were labeled and stored neatly','the workshop had a new roof','油污工具散落在地板上，所以车间显得邋遢。',1,'context'),q('What can slovenly describe besides appearance?','careless work','a type of sailing vessel','a narrow opening','slovenly 也可形容做事马虎。',1,'meaning'),q('Which workshop looks slovenly?','one with dirty tools left scattered around','one with clean tools stored by label','one with a freshly swept floor','脏工具四处乱放的车间显得 slovenly。',1,'context'),q('What does slovenly mean?','dirty or careless in appearance or work','quick to understand','quietly asleep','slovenly 指外表或做事脏乱、粗心。',1,'meaning')]);
P('slow','Slow comes from Old English slāw; it can mean not quick, not quick to understand, or become/make slower.',[C('slow.s1','慢的；缓慢的','Traffic was slow on the bridge after a lane closed, so the bus arrived ten minutes late.','一条车道关闭后桥上交通缓慢，所以公交车晚到了十分钟。','Traffic was slow on the bridge / after a lane closed / and the bus arrived late.','slow.s1 指移动、进行或发生的速度不快。','交通缓慢导致公交晚点。'),C('slow.s2','迟钝的；理解慢的','The new puzzle was difficult, but Mina was not slow; she spotted the hidden pattern before anyone else.','新谜题很难，但米娜并不迟钝；她比其他人更早发现了隐藏规律。','Mina was not slow / and spotted the hidden pattern / before anyone else.','slow.s2 用于人时可指理解或反应不快。','例句用否定形式说明米娜反应快。'),C('slow.s3','（使）慢下来','The driver slowed the van before the sharp bend to keep the tires from skidding.','司机在急弯前减慢面包车速度，避免轮胎打滑。','The driver slowed the van / before the sharp bend / to prevent skidding.','slow.s3 作动词，指速度下降或使某物速度下降。','司机在弯道前让车辆减速。')],M('Traffic was slow on the bridge, so every vehicle crossed instantly at its maximum speed.','Traffic was slow because vehicles moved at a reduced pace.','瞬间高速通过与 slow 所指的速度不快相反。','meaning'),[q('Why was traffic slow on the bridge?','a lane had closed','the bridge was newly painted','the bus had already arrived early','一条车道关闭后，桥上交通缓慢。',1,'context'),q('What did Mina do before anyone else?','spotted the hidden pattern','missed every clue because she was slow','closed a lane on the bridge','米娜先发现了隐藏规律。',1,'context'),q('Why did the driver slow the van?','to avoid skidding before a sharp bend','to make the tires lose control','to arrive before leaving the garage','司机在急弯前减速以防打滑。',1,'context'),q('What does slow mean about traffic?','moving or proceeding without speed','understanding a hidden pattern','a sudden drop in prices','slow 描述交通时指行进速度不快。',1,'meaning')]);
P('slowly','Slowly is formed from slow and -ly; it means in a way that takes time or proceeds without hurry.',C('slowly.s1','缓慢地','The nurse slowly raised the window so the sleeping patient would not be startled by the noise.','护士慢慢地抬起窗户，以免噪声惊醒熟睡的病人。','The nurse slowly raised the window / so the sleeping patient / would not be startled.','slowly.s1 指动作速度不快、从容地进行。','护士为避免惊扰病人而慢慢开窗。'),M('The nurse slowly raised the window by throwing it upward in one instant, noisy movement.','The nurse raised the window gradually and without hurry.','瞬间猛然的动作不是 slowly。','meaning'),[q('How did the nurse raise the window?','gradually and without hurry','in one instant with a loud bang','by leaving it closed','护士慢慢地抬起窗户。',1,'context'),q('Why did the nurse move slowly?','to avoid startling the sleeping patient','to wake the patient immediately','because the window was missing','护士不想惊醒病人。',1,'context'),q('What does slowly describe?','an action done without hurry','a person who is dishonest','a wet mixture of soil','slowly 表示动作进行得不急不快。',1,'meaning'),q('Which action happens slowly?','a door easing open over several seconds','a balloon bursting in a split second','a light flashing once','门在几秒内逐渐打开是 slowly。',1,'context')]);
P('slowness','Slowness is formed from slow and -ness; it means lack of speed or a delay in understanding or responding.',C('slowness.s1','缓慢；迟钝','The slowness of the old network made each file take several minutes to download.','旧网络速度太慢，每个文件都要花几分钟才能下载。','The slowness of the network / made each file / take several minutes.','slowness.s1 可指速度不足，也可指理解或反应迟缓。','网络慢使下载耗时。'),M('The slowness of the network let each huge file download instantly with no delay.','The network’s slowness made downloads take several minutes.','即时无延迟下载与 slowness 相反。','meaning'),[q('What took several minutes to download?','each file','the old network itself','the technician’s lunch','网络慢导致每个文件都要几分钟才能下载。',1,'context'),q('What does slowness mean here?','lack of speed','a sudden increase in speed','a wet mixture of sediment','这里的 slowness 指速度不足。',1,'meaning'),q('What other kind of delay can slowness describe?','a delay in understanding or responding','a bright flash of light','a short memorable phrase','slowness 也可指理解或反应迟钝。',1,'meaning'),q('Which is an example of slowness?','a person taking extra time to understand a simple instruction','a runner finishing first in record time','a machine responding instantly','理解简单指令花费额外时间体现 slowness。',1,'context')]);
P('sludge','Sludge is from Middle English slutch, “mud”; it means a heavy wet mixture of mud, sediment, or industrial residue.',C('sludge.s1','淤泥；污泥','Workers removed thick sludge from the bottom of the treatment tank before inspecting its pipes.','工人检查管道前，先清除了处理池底部厚厚的污泥。','Workers removed thick sludge / from the treatment tank / before inspecting its pipes.','sludge.s1 指泥、沉积物或工业残渣形成的稠厚湿混合物。','处理池底部积有污泥。'),M('Workers found no sludge in the tank because its bottom was dry, polished, and completely clean.','Workers removed a thick wet residue from the tank bottom.','干燥洁净的池底没有 sludge。','meaning'),[q('Where was the sludge found?','at the bottom of the treatment tank','on the roof of the workshop','inside a dry paper envelope','污泥在处理池底部。',1,'context'),q('What did workers do before inspecting pipes?','removed the thick residue','added more industrial waste','closed the treatment plant permanently','工人先清除污泥再检查管道。',1,'context'),q('What is sludge?','a heavy wet mixture of mud or residue','a short campaign phrase','a single mast on a boat','sludge 指稠厚的泥或残渣混合物。',1,'meaning'),q('Which material is sludge?','wet sediment collected from a treatment tank','clean dry sand on a beach','a thin clear sheet of glass','处理池中收集的湿沉积物是 sludge。',1,'context')]);
P('slug','Slug has several unrelated historical senses; it can name a shell-less garden creature, a heavy bullet, or a forceful punch.',[C('slug.s1','蛞蝓；鼻涕虫','A slug crossed the damp garden path, leaving a shining trail behind its soft gray body.','一只蛞蝓爬过潮湿的花园小径，在灰色软体身后留下闪亮的痕迹。','A slug crossed the damp path / leaving a shining trail / behind its body.','slug.s1 指没有外壳、身体柔软并以黏液移动的小动物。','蛞蝓在潮湿小径上爬行并留下黏液。'),C('slug.s2','弹丸；枪弹','The range officer inspected the recovered slug after the controlled test, keeping it secured as evidence.','受控测试后，靶场管理员检查了回收的弹丸，并将它作为证物妥善保管。','The officer inspected the recovered slug / after a controlled test / and secured it.','slug.s2 可指枪发射的重金属弹丸。','测试后回收了弹丸。'),C('slug.s3','猛击；重击','In the comic, the hero slugged the padded training bag once and then stepped back to rest.','在漫画里，主人公猛击了一下带衬垫的训练袋，随后退后休息。','The hero slugged the training bag / once / and stepped back.','slug.s3 作动词，指用拳头或重物狠狠击打。','主人公用力击打训练袋。')],M('The slug left no trail because the garden creature had a hard shell and never moved over damp ground.','The soft shell-less slug crossed damp ground and left a mucus trail.','有硬壳且不在潮地活动的动物不符合例句中的 slug。','meaning'),[q('What did the garden slug leave behind?','a shining trail','a metal bullet','a campaign poster','蛞蝓在小径上留下闪亮的黏液痕迹。',1,'context'),q('What did the range officer inspect?','a recovered heavy bullet','a damp garden creature','a padded training bag','管理员检查的是测试后回收的弹丸。',1,'context'),q('What did the hero do to the training bag?','hit it hard once','left a shining trail across it','secured it as evidence','主人公猛击了一下训练袋。',1,'context'),q('What does slug mean in “the hero slugged the bag”?','struck it forcefully','moved slowly on a slimy surface','a heavy metal projectile','这里 slug 作动词，表示用力击打。',3,'meaning')]);
P('sluggish','Sluggish combines slug and -ish; it means lacking energy, speed, or a quick response.',C('sluggish.s1','迟缓的；无精打采的','The sluggish laptop took nearly a minute to open a simple document after its memory filled up.','内存占满后，这台反应迟缓的笔记本电脑打开一个简单文档都要近一分钟。','The sluggish laptop took nearly a minute / to open a simple document / after its memory filled.','sluggish.s1 指缺乏速度、活力或迅速反应能力的。','电脑打开简单文件也很慢。'),M('The sluggish laptop opened every large file instantly and responded before the user clicked.','The laptop was sluggish because even a simple document took nearly a minute to open.','即时响应与 sluggish 所指的迟缓相反。','meaning'),[q('What did the laptop take nearly a minute to open?','a simple document','a large video game only','the keyboard drawer','电脑打开一个简单文档都近一分钟。',1,'context'),q('What happened to its memory?','it had filled up','it had been removed from the laptop','it became a garden path','笔记本内存占满后运行变慢。',1,'context'),q('What does sluggish mean?','lacking speed or energy','bright and shining','careless in appearance','sluggish 指迟缓、缺乏活力的。',1,'meaning'),q('Which response is sluggish?','a computer taking a long time to react to a click','a computer opening a file instantly','a person answering at once','电脑对点击反应很慢是 sluggish。',1,'context')]);
P('sluggishly','Sluggishly is formed from sluggish and -ly; it means moving or reacting without energy, as if weighed down.',C('sluggishly.s1','迟缓无力地','After the overnight freeze, the engine turned sluggishly until the oil warmed and began to circulate.','经过一夜冰冻，发动机迟缓地转动，直到机油升温并开始循环。','The engine turned sluggishly / until the oil warmed / and began to circulate.','sluggishly.s1 指动作或反应缓慢、缺乏活力地进行。','机油冷却时发动机转得迟缓。'),M('The frozen engine turned sluggishly by starting instantly at full speed with no hesitation.','The engine turned slowly and weakly while its oil was cold.','立即全速启动不属于 sluggishly。','meaning'),[q('When did the engine turn sluggishly?','after an overnight freeze','after its oil had warmed completely','while being switched off','发动机在冰冻一夜后转得迟缓。',1,'context'),q('What eventually happened to the oil?','it warmed and began to circulate','it froze permanently inside the engine','it spilled across a garden path','机油升温后开始循环。',1,'context'),q('What does sluggishly describe?','moving or reacting slowly without energy','moving with great speed','speaking in a secretive way','sluggishly 表示迟缓无力地行动或反应。',1,'meaning'),q('Which machine is turning sluggishly?','a cold engine cranking weakly before warming','a motor starting instantly at full speed','a clock running fast','冷发动机升温前无力地转动，属于 sluggishly。',1,'context')]);
P('slum','Slum is recorded in the early nineteenth century for a poor urban district; it can also be a dated colloquial verb for staying somewhere below one’s usual standard.',[C('slum.s1','贫民窟；贫民区','The city replaced unsafe housing in the slum with well-lit apartments connected to clean water and transit.','市政府用配有照明、供水和交通设施的公寓，替换了贫民区里不安全的住房。','The city replaced unsafe housing in the slum / with apartments / connected to services.','slum.s1 指城市中住房条件恶劣、居民贫困的区域。','例句以改善住房回应贫民区的居住问题。'),C('slum.s2','（口语、略带旧式）住得比平时简陋','For the field trip, the visiting professor slummed in a basic hostel rather than booking her usual hotel suite.','实地考察期间，这位来访教授住进简陋旅舍，没有预订她平常住的酒店套房。','The professor slummed in a basic hostel / rather than booking / her usual suite.','slum.s2 作动词是口语且略带旧式，指暂时住在比自己平常标准低的地方。','教授这次选择简陋旅舍，低于平日住宿标准。')],M('The city called the district a slum although every home was safe, spacious, and connected to full services.','The district was a slum because residents faced poor housing and inadequate services.','安全宽敞且设施齐全的住宅区不符合贫民区定义。','meaning'),[q('What replaced the unsafe homes in the slum?','well-lit apartments with clean water and transit','empty lots without services','private hotel suites for visitors','贫民区的不安全住房被配套公寓替换。',1,'context'),q('Where did the professor stay during the field trip?','in a basic hostel','in her usual hotel suite','in a city transit station','教授住进了简陋旅舍。',1,'context'),q('What does slum mean as a noun?','a poor urban area with bad housing','a comfortable rural resort','a sudden business decline','slum 作名词指住房条件差的城市贫民区。',1,'meaning'),q('What does the dated colloquial verb mean here?','stay somewhere below one’s usual standard','improve a neighborhood’s services','inspect unsafe housing','此处 slum 作动词指暂住在比平时简陋的地方。',1,'meaning')]);
P('slumber','Slumber comes from Old English slǣmerian; it can be a gentle or literary noun for sleep or a verb meaning to sleep peacefully.',[C('slumber.s1','睡眠；安睡','A brief slumber on the train refreshed Nia before she reached the mountain station.','在火车上短暂睡了一会儿，让妮娅抵达山站前恢复了精神。','A brief slumber on the train / refreshed Nia / before the mountain station.','slumber.s1 作名词，指睡眠，语气较温和或文学化。','短暂睡眠让她恢复精神。'),C('slumber.s2','睡；安睡','The village seemed to slumber beneath fresh snow while only the bakery chimney released a thin curl of smoke.','新雪覆盖下，村庄仿佛在安睡，只有面包房烟囱冒出一缕细烟。','The village seemed to slumber / beneath fresh snow / while the bakery chimney smoked.','slumber.s2 作动词，指睡觉，常带安静、平和的意味。','安静雪景中村庄如同沉睡。')],M('Nia took a brief slumber on the train by staying fully awake and alert for the entire journey.','Nia slept briefly on the train and felt refreshed afterward.','始终清醒不属于 slumber。','meaning'),[q('Where did Nia have a brief slumber?','on the train','in the bakery chimney','on a garden path','妮娅在火车上短暂睡了一会儿。',1,'context'),q('How did she feel afterward?','refreshed','more tired because she never slept','angry at the village','短暂睡眠让妮娅恢复了精神。',1,'context'),q('What does slumber mean as a noun?','sleep','a heavy punch','a poor city district','slumber 作名词指睡眠。',1,'meaning'),q('What does “the village seemed to slumber” suggest?','the village was quiet and still, as if asleep','the village was crowded and noisy','the village was being rebuilt','这句话把安静的村庄描写成仿佛正在安睡。',1,'meaning')]);
P('slump','Slump may come from a Scandinavian source meaning fall heavily; it can mean fall sharply, sit/fall heavily, or a period of economic decline.',[C('slump.s1','暴跌；急剧下降','Sales slumped after the shop moved away from the busy station and lost most passing customers.','商店搬离繁忙车站、失去多数过路顾客后，销售额骤降。','Sales slumped / after the shop moved / away from the busy station.','slump.s1 作动词，指数量、价格或水平突然大幅下降。','失去客流后销售额急剧下滑。'),C('slump.s2','重重坐下；瘫倒','Exhausted after the hike, Ben slumped into the chair and let his backpack fall beside him.','徒步后筋疲力尽的本重重地瘫坐进椅子，把背包放在一旁。','Ben slumped into the chair / after the hike / and dropped his backpack beside him.','slump.s2 指因疲惫等原因沉重地坐下或倒下。','本疲惫地瘫进椅子。'),C('slump.s3','萧条；低迷期','The region’s housing slump lasted two years, with few homes selling and prices falling steadily.','当地房地产低迷持续了两年，房屋成交寥寥，价格持续下跌。','The housing slump lasted two years / with few homes selling / and prices falling.','slump.s3 作名词，指经济、销售等持续低迷或下降的一段时期。','房屋成交少且价格下跌形成市场低迷期。')],M('Sales slumped after the move, meaning the shop sold more than ever and its income rose sharply.','Sales slumped because the shop lost passing customers and its sales fell.','销量大幅增长与 slump 所指的骤降相反。','meaning'),[q('Why did the shop’s sales slump?','it moved away from the busy station and lost passing customers','it opened beside a crowded station','it lowered every price to zero','搬离车站后失去过路顾客，导致销量骤降。',1,'context'),q('Where did Ben slump?','into a chair after the hike','onto a boat’s mast','under a shop sign','本徒步后重重地瘫坐进椅子。',2,'context'),q('How long did the housing slump last?','two years','two days','ten decades','当地房地产低迷持续了两年。',3,'context'),q('What does slump mean in “a housing slump”?','a period of falling activity and prices','a brief sleep','a steep hillside','housing slump 指房地产活动低迷、价格下跌的一段时期。',3,'meaning')]);
P('slur','Slur comes from an older verb meaning to speak indistinctly; it can mean an insulting remark, make such an insult, or speak unclearly.',[C('slur.s1','侮辱性言辞；诽谤','The referee apologized after an offensive slur about the visiting team was heard from the stands.','看台上传出针对客队的侮辱性言辞后，裁判作出了道歉。','The referee apologized / after an offensive slur / was heard from the stands.','slur.s1 指侮辱个人或群体的言辞，尤其涉及身份或背景时。','看台上传出针对客队的侮辱话语。'),C('slur.s2','侮辱；中伤','It is unfair to slur a colleague’s reputation without checking whether the accusation is true.','未经核实指控是否属实就中伤同事名誉是不公平的。','It is unfair to slur a colleague’s reputation / without checking / the accusation.','slur.s2 作动词，指不公正地侮辱或诋毁某人的名誉。','未经核实就诋毁同事。'),C('slur.s3','含糊不清地说','Because the medicine made him drowsy, the patient began to slur his words during the telephone call.','药物使病人昏昏欲睡，所以他在通话时开始含糊不清地说话。','The patient began to slur his words / during the telephone call / because medicine made him drowsy.','slur.s3 指因醉酒、疲倦或疾病而说话含混。','药物导致嗜睡，说话含混。')],M('The patient slurred his words clearly, pronouncing every syllable slowly and distinctly.','The patient slurred his words because drowsiness made his speech unclear.','清晰地逐音节发音与 slur 的含糊说话义相反。','meaning'),[q('What did the referee hear from the stands?','an offensive slur about the visiting team','a neutral weather report','a quiet bedtime story','看台上传出针对客队的侮辱性言辞。',1,'context'),q('What should be checked before making a claim about a colleague?','whether the accusation is true','whether the colleague owns a boat','whether the referee heard it','应先核实指控是否属实。',1,'context'),q('Why did the patient slur his words?','medicine made him drowsy','he was reading a clear script','the telephone had no sound','药物使病人昏沉，导致说话含混。',1,'context'),q('What does slur mean as a verb in the patient example?','speak unclearly','insult a group','fall sharply in price','病人例句中的 slur 指含糊不清地说话。',3,'meaning')]);
P('slurry','Slurry is related to slur and denotes a wet mixture; it means a semi-liquid blend of water and small solid particles.',C('slurry.s1','浆料；泥浆','The crew pumped a cement slurry through the hose to fill gaps beneath the new foundation.','施工队把水泥浆料泵入软管，填充新地基下方的空隙。','The crew pumped cement slurry / through the hose / beneath the foundation.','slurry.s1 指由水和细小固体颗粒组成的半液态混合物。','水泥浆可流入地基缝隙。'),M('The crew used cement slurry that was completely dry, solid, and unable to flow through the hose.','The crew pumped a semi-liquid cement mixture through the hose.','完全干燥而不能流动的材料不是 slurry。','meaning'),[q('What did the crew pump through the hose?','cement slurry','dry gravel only','a garden slug','施工队把水泥浆料泵入软管。',1,'context'),q('Where was the slurry sent?','beneath the new foundation','onto a campaign poster','into a bedroom window','浆料被送到新地基下方填缝。',1,'context'),q('What is slurry?','a semi-liquid mixture of water and small solids','a dry metal bullet','a single open hand hit','slurry 指水与细小固体颗粒组成的半液态混合物。',1,'meaning'),q('Which substance is a slurry?','water mixed with fine cement particles so it can be pumped','a block of fully cured dry concrete','pure water with no particles','可泵送的水泥细颗粒混合液是 slurry。',1,'context')]);
P('slush','Slush is related to slosh and means wet, dirty snow that is melting on the ground.',C('slush.s1','半融雪；雪泥','After the thaw, gray slush collected along the curb and splashed onto the passing bicycles.','解冻后，灰色雪泥堆在路沿边，溅到了经过的自行车上。','Gray slush collected along the curb / after the thaw / and splashed onto bicycles.','slush.s1 指地面上正在融化、又湿又脏的雪。','解冻后的雪水泥泞并飞溅。'),M('Gray slush collected along the curb even though the snow was dry, powdery, and frozen solid.','Gray wet snowmelt gathered along the curb and splashed onto passing bicycles.','干燥蓬松且冻硬的雪不是 slush。','meaning'),[q('Where did the gray slush collect?','along the curb','on the roof of the bus','inside the bicycle tires','灰色雪泥堆在路沿边。',1,'context'),q('What did the slush splash onto?','passing bicycles','the bakery chimney','a paper invitation','雪泥溅到了经过的自行车上。',1,'context'),q('What does slush mean?','wet, dirty melting snow','clean powdery snow','thick industrial oil','slush 指正在融化的湿脏雪泥。',1,'meaning'),q('Which street surface is covered in slush?','gray melting snow mixed with water and dirt','dry clean pavement in summer','a thin layer of ice with no water','混有水和泥土的灰色融雪是 slush。',1,'context')]);
P('sluttish','Sluttish is an older adjective from slut; it means dirty and careless in dress or housekeeping, and is now dated and often offensive when applied to people.',C('sluttish.s1','（旧用法）邋遢的；不整洁的','The nineteenth-century diary called the untidy kitchen “sluttish,” a dated judgment the modern editor flagged as derogatory.','十九世纪日记把凌乱的厨房称作“邋遢”，现代编辑指出这种评价已过时且带贬义。','The diary called the kitchen “sluttish” / a dated judgment / flagged as derogatory.','sluttish.s1 是旧式形容词，指衣着或家务不整洁；用于人时常带冒犯性，应谨慎理解。','日记中的词形反映时代用语，现代编辑特别标注其贬义。'),M('The diary used sluttish as a neutral compliment for a spotless, carefully arranged kitchen.','The dated diary used sluttish critically for an untidy kitchen.','该词旧用法是贬抑凌乱，并非称赞整洁。','meaning'),[q('What did the diary call “sluttish”?','the untidy kitchen','the spotless and carefully arranged kitchen','the modern editor','日记用 sluttish 描写凌乱的厨房。',1,'context'),q('How did the modern editor treat the word?','flagged it as dated and derogatory','recommended it as a polite compliment','translated it as a neutral job title','现代编辑指出该词过时且带贬义。',1,'context'),q('What did sluttish mean in the old usage?','dirty or careless in dress or housekeeping','quietly asleep','very slow to react','sluttish 的旧用法指衣着或家务邋遢。',1,'meaning'),q('Why should the word be used cautiously about a person?','it is dated and often offensive','it always expresses praise','it is a technical word for a kitchen','该词用于人时常带冒犯性，所以应谨慎。',1,'meaning')]);
P('sly','Sly comes from Middle English; it can mean secretly clever at deceiving people or, of a look/joke, quietly knowing and secretive.',[C('sly.s1','狡猾的；诡诈的','The sly contractor hid extra charges in the final page of the contract, hoping clients would miss them.','狡猾的承包商把额外费用藏在合同最后一页，希望客户不会发现。','The sly contractor hid extra charges / on the final page / hoping clients would miss them.','sly.s1 形容人时指暗中耍手段、善于欺骗的。','承包商把费用藏起来让客户漏看。'),C('sly.s2','暗中的；会心的','When the magician revealed the hidden card, her assistant gave the audience a sly smile.','魔术师揭示藏起来的牌时，助手向观众露出会意而神秘的微笑。','Her assistant gave the audience a sly smile / when the hidden card / was revealed.','sly.s2 形容神情或玩笑时，指带有不明说的会意、秘密意味。','助手的微笑暗示他知道秘密。')],M('The sly contractor made every charge obvious on the first page and encouraged clients to check it.','The sly contractor concealed extra fees where clients might overlook them.','主动突出并提醒检查费用，不符合 sly 的欺骗性。','meaning'),[q('Where did the contractor hide the extra charges?','on the final page of the contract','on the first page in large print','on the workshop floor','承包商把额外费用藏在合同最后一页。',1,'context'),q('What did the assistant do when the card appeared?','gave the audience a sly smile','hid the contract charges','fell asleep on the train','助手露出会意而神秘的微笑。',2,'context'),q('What does sly mean about the contractor?','secretly clever at deceiving clients','openly honest and careful','slow because of a cold engine','sly 描述承包商时指狡猾、暗中欺骗。',1,'meaning'),q('What can a sly smile suggest?','a quiet, knowing secret','an openly confused expression','a painful injury','sly smile 可表示带有秘密意味、心照不宣的笑。',2,'meaning')]);
P('smack','Smack may be imitative of the sound of a sharp blow; it can mean an open-hand hit, hit with a flat hand/heavy object, or the sharp sound of impact.',[C('smack.s1','（打脸的）一巴掌','The actor’s slapstick scene ended with a theatrical smack on the padded cheek, followed by a comic gasp.','演员的滑稽场景以一记打在有衬垫脸颊上的夸张巴掌结束，随后传来滑稽的倒吸气声。','The scene ended with a theatrical smack / on the padded cheek / followed by a comic gasp.','smack.s1 作名词，指尤其打在脸上的响亮手掌击打。','衬垫和夸张表演显示这是舞台效果。'),C('smack.s2','拍打；重击','The waves smacked the side of the pier during the storm, sending spray over the railing.','暴风雨中海浪拍打码头侧面，浪花越过栏杆飞溅。','The waves smacked the pier / during the storm / sending spray over the railing.','smack.s2 作动词，指用平面或重物用力击打。','海浪用力撞击码头。'),C('smack.s3','啪的一声；撞击声','A book fell flat onto the desk with a loud smack that stopped the room’s conversation.','一本书平着掉到桌上，啪的一声让房间里的谈话停了下来。','A book fell flat onto the desk / with a loud smack / that stopped the conversation.','smack.s3 指物体用力撞击表面时发出的清脆响声。','书落桌发出啪的一声。')],M('The waves smacked the pier while remaining far away and never touching any surface.','The waves struck the pier hard and threw spray over its railing.','完全没有接触不可能产生 smack 的撞击。','meaning'),[q('What followed the actor’s theatrical smack?','a comic gasp','a quiet weather report','a falling tide chart','演员夸张地打了一巴掌后，传来滑稽的倒吸气声。',1,'context'),q('What did the waves do to the pier?','struck its side and sent spray over the railing','stayed far away without touching it','covered it with dry paper','海浪拍打码头，浪花越过栏杆。',2,'context'),q('What made the loud smack on the desk?','a book falling flat','a wave reaching the mountain','a quiet conversation','书平着掉到桌上，发出啪的一声。',3,'context'),q('What is a smack in the sound example?','a sharp noise from an impact','a soft sustained hum','a slow drop in sales','这里的 smack 指物体撞击表面发出的清脆响声。',3,'meaning')]);
P('small','Small comes from Old English smæl; it means not large in size or amount, and can also describe something as unimportant.',[C('small.s1','小的；少的','A small paper label was enough to identify each jar in the crowded pantry.','一张小纸标签就足以区分拥挤储藏室里的每个罐子。','A small paper label / was enough / to identify each jar.','small.s1 指尺寸、数量或程度不大。','标签尺寸很小。'),C('small.s2','不重要的；微不足道的','The chairperson said the typo was a small matter and asked the group to focus on the safety issue.','主席说这个拼写错误只是小事，并请大家把注意力放在安全问题上。','The chairperson called the typo a small matter / and asked the group / to focus on safety.','small.s2 指重要性不高、无关紧要的事。','与安全问题相比，拼写错误不重要。')],M('The chairperson called the typo small because it was the most serious threat to everyone’s safety.','The chairperson treated the typo as unimportant beside the safety issue.','最严重的安全威胁不能称为 small matter。','meaning'),[q('What was the small label used for?','identifying each jar','covering the whole pantry door','measuring the room’s temperature','小标签用来区分每个罐子。',1,'context'),q('What did the chairperson call a small matter?','the typo','the safety issue','the crowded pantry','主席把拼写错误称为小事。',1,'context'),q('What does small mean about the label?','not large in size','very important','difficult to read aloud','small 描述标签时指尺寸不大。',1,'meaning'),q('What does small mean in “a small matter”?','unimportant or minor','physically tiny','lower in number than before','small matter 指不重要的小事。',1,'meaning')]);
P('small-scale','Small-scale combines small and scale; it describes an activity involving fewer people or things than usual, or a reduced-size model.',[C('small-scale.s1','小规模的','The cooperative began with a small-scale trial on two farms before offering the seed program across the region.','合作社先在两家农场开展小规模试验，之后才把种子项目推广到全地区。','The cooperative began with a small-scale trial / on two farms / before regional expansion.','small-scale.s1 指参与者或活动规模比通常情况小。','只在两家农场先行试验。'),C('small-scale.s2','小型的；缩小比例的','The museum displayed a small-scale model of the bridge, preserving its shape while fitting on a table.','博物馆展出了一座按比例缩小的桥梁模型，保留原有形状且能放在桌上。','The museum displayed a small-scale model / preserving the bridge’s shape / on a table.','small-scale.s2 指保持原形而尺寸缩小的模型或复制品。','模型形状相同但尺寸缩小。')],M('The cooperative called its small-scale trial regional because it already involved every farm in the country.','The trial was small-scale because it initially involved only two farms.','仅两家农场参与，说明试验规模有限。','meaning'),[q('How many farms joined the initial trial?','two','twenty thousand','none; it was only a museum model','初期试验只在两家农场开展。',1,'context'),q('What made the bridge model small-scale?','it kept the shape but fit on a table','it was larger than the real bridge','it included every bridge in the region','模型保留桥的形状，但尺寸缩小到可放桌上。',2,'context'),q('What does small-scale mean about the trial?','involving fewer participants or activities than usual','taking place across every country','having no limits on size','small-scale 描述试验时指规模有限。',1,'meaning'),q('What does small-scale mean about the model?','made smaller while keeping the same shape','built at full size','drawn without preserving proportions','small-scale model 指形状保持一致、尺寸缩小的模型。',2,'meaning')]);
P('smaller','Smaller is the comparative form of small; it means less in size, amount, or importance, or a lower number than before.',[C('smaller.s1','（尺寸、程度）更小的','The smaller suitcase fit under the train seat, while the larger case had to go in the luggage rack.','较小的手提箱能放进火车座位下方，而较大的箱子只能放在行李架上。','The smaller suitcase fit under the seat / while the larger case / went on the rack.','smaller.s1 比较尺寸、数量或重要性时，表示相对更小。','较小的箱子能放在座位下。'),C('smaller.s2','（数量）更少的','After the club stopped printing paper flyers, it needed a smaller number of volunteers for distribution.','俱乐部停止印制纸质传单后，分发工作需要的志愿者人数减少了。','The club needed a smaller number of volunteers / after it stopped / printing flyers.','smaller.s2 可表示人数或其他可数事物的数量比之前少。','停止印传单后所需志愿者更少。')],M('The smaller suitcase was larger than the other case and could not fit under the seat.','The smaller suitcase was less large and fit beneath the train seat.','能放入座位下的是尺寸较小的行李箱。','meaning'),[q('Where did the smaller suitcase fit?','under the train seat','on the roof of the train','inside the larger case','较小的手提箱放进了座位下方。',1,'context'),q('What happened to volunteer needs after the club stopped printing flyers?','the number needed became lower','the number doubled','no volunteers were ever needed','俱乐部停止印传单后，需要的志愿者人数减少。',2,'context'),q('What does smaller mean about the suitcase?','less in physical size than the other case','more expensive than the train','lower in number than before','smaller 描述手提箱时指尺寸更小。',1,'meaning'),q('What does smaller mean in “a smaller number of volunteers”?','fewer people','shorter people','people with smaller suitcases','smaller number 指人数更少。',1,'meaning')]);
P('smallholder','Smallholder combines small and holder; it means a person who owns or rents a small plot to grow crops or keep animals.',C('smallholder.s1','小农；小农场主','A smallholder near the village grows beans on two acres and keeps a few goats for milk.','村旁的一位小农在两英亩地上种豆，还养了几只山羊产奶。','A smallholder grows beans on two acres / and keeps a few goats / for milk.','smallholder.s1 指拥有或租用小块土地、从事种植或养殖的人。','种植豆类并养少量山羊符合小农经营。'),M('The smallholder managed thousands of hectares and employed an army of workers on a vast estate.','The smallholder farmed a small plot and kept only a few animals.','大面积庄园与 smallholder 的小规模土地经营不符。','meaning'),[q('What did the smallholder grow?','beans','rice in a city factory','flowers on a ship','小农在两英亩地上种豆。',1,'context'),q('Which animals did the smallholder keep?','a few goats for milk','a herd of elephants','no animals at all','他养了几只山羊产奶。',1,'context'),q('What is a smallholder?','a person farming a small piece of land','the owner of a vast estate','a worker who repairs smartphones','smallholder 指经营小块土地的农户。',1,'meaning'),q('Which person is a smallholder?','someone renting a small plot to grow vegetables','someone managing thousands of hectares','someone selling tickets at a station','租小块地种菜的人是 smallholder。',1,'context')]);
P('smallpox','Smallpox is formed from small and pox; it was a contagious viral disease marked by fever and pus-filled spots, now eradicated through vaccination.',C('smallpox.s1','天花','Historical records describe a smallpox outbreak in which fever and fluid-filled spots left scars among survivors.','历史记录描述了一次天花疫情，患者发热并出现脓疱，幸存者身上留下疤痕。','Records describe a smallpox outbreak / with fever and spots / that left scars.','smallpox.s1 指曾造成发热和脓疱的传染性病毒病；该病已通过疫苗接种根除。','例句写到典型病征及疤痕。'),M('The smallpox outbreak caused no fever or spots and spread only through inherited genes.','The historical outbreak involved contagious smallpox with fever and pus-filled spots.','天花是传染性疾病，常伴发热和脓疱，并非遗传病。','meaning'),[q('What symptoms did the records mention?','fever and fluid-filled spots','a cough with no skin symptoms','only a sore throat','记录提到发热和脓疱。',1,'context'),q('What could remain after survivors recovered?','scars','a metal fragment','a phone application','幸存者可能留下疤痕。',1,'context'),q('What was smallpox?','a contagious viral disease','a harmless crop fungus','a type of farming tool','smallpox 是传染性病毒病天花。',1,'meaning'),q('What is true of smallpox today?','it was eradicated through vaccination','it is a common seasonal cold','it is inherited but not contagious','天花已通过疫苗接种被根除。',1,'meaning')]);
P('smart','Smart comes from Old English smeart, originally “painful/sharp”; it can mean quick to understand, neat or fashionable/technology-enabled, or feel a sharp pain.',[C('smart.s1','聪明的；机敏的','Even with little time, the smart apprentice identified the faulty wire by comparing the circuit diagrams.','尽管时间不多，这名机敏的学徒仍通过比较电路图找到了故障电线。','The smart apprentice identified the faulty wire / by comparing diagrams / despite little time.','smart.s1 指学习和理解迅速、判断机敏的。','学徒很快根据图纸找出故障。'),C('smart.s2','整齐时髦的；智能的','She wore a smart jacket to the interview and checked the directions on her smart watch.','她穿着整洁时髦的夹克去面试，并用智能手表查看路线。','She wore a smart jacket / and checked directions / on her smart watch.','smart.s2 可形容整洁时髦，也可指由计算机控制或联网的智能设备。','同一句展示衣着和智能设备用法。'),C('smart.s3','感到刺痛','The cut began to smart when salt water touched the skin, so he rinsed it with clean water.','盐水碰到皮肤时伤口开始刺痛，于是他用清水冲洗。','The cut began to smart / when salt water touched it / so he rinsed the skin.','smart.s3 作动词，指感到突然的刺痛。','盐水刺激伤口产生刺痛。')],M('The cut began to smart when the anesthetic made the skin completely numb and painless.','The cut smarted because salt water caused a sudden sharp pain.','完全麻木无痛与 smart 的刺痛义相反。','meaning'),[q('How did the apprentice find the faulty wire?','by comparing circuit diagrams','by guessing without looking','by checking a farming field','学徒比较电路图后找到了故障电线。',1,'context'),q('What did she wear to the interview?','a smart jacket','a muddy work apron','a sleeping bag','她穿着整洁时髦的夹克参加面试。',1,'context'),q('What happened when salt water touched the cut?','it began to smart','it became a smart watch','it healed instantly without sensation','盐水碰到伤口后开始刺痛。',1,'context'),q('What does smart mean about the apprentice?','quick to learn and understand','neatly dressed','feeling a sharp pain','smart 描述学徒时指聪明机敏。',1,'meaning')]);
P('smarten','Smarten is formed from smart and -en; it means improve the appearance of a person, room, or object.',C('smarten.s1','使整洁；使更漂亮','Before the open house, the landlord painted the doorway and added flowers to smarten the front room.','开放参观前，房东粉刷门廊并摆上鲜花，让前厅更整洁好看。','The landlord added flowers to smarten the front room / before the open house / and painted the doorway.','smarten.s1 指通过整理、装饰或修补改善外观。','鲜花和新漆让房间更美观。'),M('The landlord smartened the room by removing its paint, scattering rubbish, and hiding every flower.','The landlord improved the room’s appearance with fresh paint and flowers.','增加破败和杂乱不会使房间更整洁美观。','meaning'),[q('What did the landlord add to the front room?','flowers','industrial sludge','broken glass','房东在前厅摆上鲜花。',1,'context'),q('Why did the landlord prepare the room?','for an open house','for a smelting test','to store dirty snow','房东在开放参观前整理房间。',1,'context'),q('What does smarten mean?','improve the appearance of something','make a computer respond slowly','strike a surface sharply','smarten 指改善外观、使更整洁漂亮。',1,'meaning'),q('Which action would smarten a hallway?','painting the walls and clearing clutter','spreading mud across the floor','removing all lights','粉刷墙壁并清理杂物会让走廊更整洁。',1,'context')]);
P('smartphone','Smartphone combines smart and phone; it means a mobile phone with computer functions for internet access and applications.',C('smartphone.s1','智能手机','A smartphone let the survey team upload field photographs and check digital maps while far from the office.','智能手机让调查队在远离办公室时上传实地照片并查看电子地图。','A smartphone let the survey team upload photos / and check digital maps / far from the office.','smartphone.s1 指具备计算功能、能联网并运行应用程序的手机。','手机在野外支持上传照片和查看地图。'),M('The survey team used a smartphone that could make calls only and had no computer functions, internet, or apps.','The smartphone connected to the internet and ran map and photo applications.','能联网并运行应用的手机不只是普通语音电话。','meaning'),[q('What did the survey team upload?','field photographs','printed farming leases','a metal bullet','调查队用手机上传实地照片。',1,'context'),q('What did they check on the phone?','digital maps','the engine oil level','a paper-only timetable','他们在手机上查看电子地图。',1,'context'),q('What is a smartphone?','a mobile phone with computer functions and apps','a phone that can make calls only','a small farm plot','smartphone 指带有计算功能和应用程序的手机。',1,'meaning'),q('Why was the smartphone useful far from the office?','it could connect the team with digital maps and uploads','it worked only when fixed to an office desk','it replaced every field surveyor','它能在野外查看地图并上传照片，因此很有用。',1,'context')]);
P('smash','Smash is probably imitative of a crashing sound; it can mean break violently, hit very hard, or a crash/a highly successful entertainment event.',[C('smash.s1','打碎；撞毁','A gust knocked the empty bottle from the shelf, and it smashed on the stone floor.','一阵风把空瓶从架子上吹落，瓶子在石地板上摔碎了。','The bottle smashed on the stone floor / after a gust / knocked it down.','smash.s1 作动词，指猛烈撞击并碎裂或毁坏。','瓶子撞到石地板后碎裂。'),C('smash.s2','猛击；扣杀','At the final point, the tennis player smashed the ball past her opponent and won the match.','赛点时，网球选手猛力扣球越过对手，赢下比赛。','The player smashed the ball / past her opponent / at the final point.','smash.s2 作动词，指用力猛击；在网球等运动中也指扣球。','选手用力扣球得分。'),C('smash.s3','撞车；轰动成功','The touring band’s first album was a smash, selling out venues across the country.','巡演乐队的首张专辑大获成功，在全国各地的演出场馆都一票售罄。','The first album was a smash / and sold out venues / across the country.','smash.s3 作名词可指猛烈碰撞，也可口语表示极成功的作品或演出。','专辑热销且演出门票售罄。')],M('The bottle smashed on the stone floor but remained whole and uncracked.','The bottle broke into pieces when it hit the stone floor.','保持完整未裂与 smash 的猛烈破碎义相反。','meaning'),[q('What caused the bottle to fall?','a gust','a tennis player','a successful album','一阵风把瓶子从架子上吹落。',1,'context'),q('How did the tennis player score the final point?','by smashing the ball past her opponent','by dropping the ball outside the court','by breaking her racket','选手猛力扣球越过对手赢下比赛。',1,'context'),q('Why was the album called a smash?','it was highly successful and venues sold out','it broke into physical pieces','it contained no songs','专辑大获成功，演出门票售罄。',1,'context'),q('What does smash mean in the bottle example?','break violently into pieces','a neat appearance','a phone with internet access','瓶子例句中的 smash 指猛烈撞碎。',1,'meaning')]);
P('smear','Smear is from Middle English smeren, “to rub or anoint”; it can mean spread a wet substance, a dirty mark/thin coating, or an unfair damaging claim.',[C('smear.s1','涂抹；抹上','The technician smeared a thin layer of gel over the sensor before recording the measurements.','技术员在记录测量数据前，把一层薄凝胶涂在传感器上。','The technician smeared gel over the sensor / before recording / the measurements.','smear.s1 作动词，指将柔软或湿的物质不均匀地抹在表面上。','凝胶被涂抹在传感器上。'),C('smear.s2','污迹；涂层','A gray smear on the window showed where the mechanic had wiped an oily glove.','窗上的灰色污迹表明修理工曾用沾油的手套擦过那里。','A gray smear on the window / showed where / an oily glove wiped.','smear.s2 作名词，指抹开物质留下的污迹或薄层。','油手套在玻璃上留下污迹。'),C('smear.s3','诽谤；中伤','The candidate called the fabricated accusation a smear designed to damage her reputation.','候选人称这项捏造的指控是旨在损害她名誉的诽谤。','The candidate called the false accusation a smear / designed to damage / her reputation.','smear.s3 指意在损害名誉的不实、不公平说法。','捏造指控被称为诽谤。')],M('The candidate called the smear fair and accurate because every claim had been independently verified.','The candidate called the fabricated, reputation-damaging accusation a smear.','经过独立核实的准确事实并非诽谤。','meaning'),[q('What did the technician smear on the sensor?','a thin layer of gel','a dry sheet of paper','a heavy metal projectile','技术员在传感器上涂了一层薄凝胶。',1,'context'),q('How was the gray mark on the window made?','an oily glove wiped the glass','a clean cloth polished it dry','the sensor uploaded data','修理工用沾油手套擦玻璃留下污迹。',1,'context'),q('Why did the candidate call the accusation a smear?','it was fabricated to damage her reputation','it was independently verified and fair','it was a thin coating of gel','候选人认为指控是捏造出来损害名誉的。',1,'context'),q('What does smear mean in the political example?','an unfair damaging statement','a layer of gel spread on a surface','a polite compliment','这里的 smear 指诽谤或中伤。',1,'meaning')]);
P('smell','Smell comes from Old English smell; it can mean notice with the nose, have a particular odor, or an odor/the sense of smelling.',[C('smell.s1','闻到；嗅出','The guard smelled smoke beneath the door and called the fire service before entering the room.','警卫闻到门下有烟味，便在进入房间前呼叫消防人员。','The guard smelled smoke / beneath the door / and called the fire service.','smell.s1 作动词，指用鼻子察觉或发现气味。','警卫通过嗅觉发现烟。'),C('smell.s2','有……气味','The soup smells of ginger and lime after the cook adds the fresh ingredients.','厨师加入新鲜食材后，汤闻起来有姜和青柠的香味。','The soup smells of ginger and lime / after the cook / adds fresh ingredients.','smell.s2 作系动词，指具有某种可闻到的气味。','汤具有姜和青柠的气味。'),C('smell.s3','气味；嗅觉','The smell of wet earth after rain reminded the hikers of the garden behind their childhood home.','雨后湿土的气味让徒步者想起童年家后面的花园。','The smell of wet earth / reminded the hikers / of their childhood garden.','smell.s3 作名词可指气味，也可指嗅觉。','雨后湿土的气味引发回忆。')],M('The guard smelled smoke but detected nothing with his nose and never noticed any odor.','The guard detected smoke by its odor beneath the door.','完全没有察觉气味与 smell 的嗅出义相反。','meaning'),[q('What did the guard smell beneath the door?','smoke','ginger and lime soup','wet earth after rain','警卫闻到门下有烟味。',1,'context'),q('What did the soup smell of?','ginger and lime','smoke and metal','wet snow','汤闻起来有姜和青柠的香味。',2,'context'),q('What reminded the hikers of home?','the smell of wet earth after rain','the sound of a tennis match','a clean window','雨后湿土的气味让徒步者想起家。',3,'context'),q('What does smell mean as a noun in the final example?','an odor noticed by the nose','the act of breaking a bottle','a phone application','此处 smell 作名词指气味。',3,'meaning')]);
P('smelly','Smelly is formed from smell and -y; it describes something giving off an odor that people notice and often dislike.',C('smelly.s1','有臭味的','The smelly compost bin was moved away from the kitchen door and covered with a tight lid.','有臭味的堆肥桶被移到厨房门外较远处，并盖上严密的盖子。','The smelly compost bin was moved away / from the kitchen door / and covered.','smelly.s1 指散发出明显且常令人不喜欢的气味。','堆肥桶的气味让人远离厨房。'),M('The smelly bin gave off a fresh, pleasant scent that everyone wanted near the dining table.','The bin had a strong unpleasant odor, so it was moved away from the kitchen.','令人喜欢的清香与 smelly 通常含有的难闻气味相反。','meaning'),[q('What was moved away from the kitchen door?','the compost bin','the dining table','a clean flower vase','有臭味的堆肥桶被移开。',1,'context'),q('What was done to the bin?','it was covered with a tight lid','it was placed beside the dining table','it was filled with fresh flowers','桶被盖上了严密的盖子。',1,'context'),q('What does smelly mean?','giving off an odor people often dislike','having no odor at all','looking untidy but smelling sweet','smelly 指散发出常令人不喜欢的气味。',1,'meaning'),q('Which item is smelly?','a spoiled-food container with a strong bad odor','a sealed clean jar with no scent','a fresh lemon that smells pleasant','发出浓烈坏味的腐坏食物桶是 smelly。',1,'context')]);
P('smelter','Smelter is formed from smelt and -er; it means a furnace, works, or worker that extracts metal from ore by heating.',C('smelter.s1','冶炼炉；冶炼厂；冶炼工','The smelter heated copper ore until the molten metal separated from the unwanted rock.','冶炼炉加热铜矿石，直到熔融金属与废石分离。','The smelter heated copper ore / until molten metal separated / from waste rock.','smelter.s1 可指从矿石中加热提取金属的炉、工厂或工人。','高温使铜与废石分离。'),M('The smelter extracted copper by keeping the ore cold so no metal could melt or separate.','The smelter heated ore until the metal separated from waste rock.','冶炼通过加热分离金属，冷却矿石无法完成该过程。','meaning'),[q('What did the smelter heat?','copper ore','a smartphone battery only','wet snow','冶炼炉加热的是铜矿石。',1,'context'),q('What separated from the waste rock?','molten metal','a paper label','a garden slug','熔融金属与废石分离。',1,'context'),q('What is a smelter?','a furnace, works, or worker that extracts metal from ore','a machine that measures phone signals','a person who farms a small plot','smelter 指通过加热矿石提取金属的炉、厂或工人。',1,'meaning'),q('Which process takes place at a smelter?','heating ore to separate metal from waste rock','freezing soup to create a smell','shaping a small paper label','在冶炼炉中加热矿石，使金属与废石分离。',1,'meaning')]);
P('smelting','Smelting is formed from smelt and -ing; it is the industrial heating process that separates metal from waste rock in ore.',C('smelting.s1','冶炼','Smelting the iron ore in a furnace separated usable metal from the surrounding mineral waste.','在炉中冶炼铁矿石，把可用金属与周围矿物废料分离开来。','Smelting the iron ore / separated usable metal / from mineral waste.','smelting.s1 指加热矿石、使金属与废石分离的工业过程。','矿石经高温处理后提取铁。'),M('Smelting separated iron from its ore by keeping the furnace cold and preventing any material from heating.','Smelting heats ore in a furnace so metal separates from waste rock.','冶炼以加热为核心，冷炉不能分离金属。','meaning'),[q('What did smelting separate from mineral waste?','usable iron','water from a snowbank','a paper invitation','冶炼把可用铁从矿物废料中分离。',1,'context'),q('Where did the process happen?','in a furnace','in a refrigerator','on a garden path','冶炼过程在炉中进行。',1,'context'),q('What is smelting?','industrial heating that extracts metal from ore','the act of polishing a window','a method of growing crops on a small plot','smelting 指加热矿石以提取金属的工业过程。',1,'meaning'),q('Which activity is smelting?','heating ore until metal separates from waste rock','cooling a soup until it freezes','sorting labels by size','加热矿石并分离金属与废石属于 smelting。',1,'context')]);
P('smile','Smile comes from Old English smilian; it can mean make the corners of the mouth turn up or the resulting facial expression.',[C('smile.s1','微笑','The child smiled when the familiar dog returned to the gate, wagging its tail.','熟悉的小狗摇着尾巴回到门口时，孩子笑了。','The child smiled / when the familiar dog returned / wagging its tail.','smile.s1 作动词，指嘴角上扬以表达愉悦、友善等。','小狗回来让孩子开心地笑。'),C('smile.s2','笑容','A tired but genuine smile appeared on the nurse’s face when the last patient went home safely.','最后一位病人平安回家时，护士疲惫但真诚的笑容浮现在脸上。','A genuine smile appeared / on the nurse’s face / when the patient went home safely.','smile.s2 作名词，指嘴角上扬形成的表情。','护士脸上出现笑容。')],M('The child smiled at the dog by frowning, turning away, and refusing to look at it.','The child’s mouth turned up in a smile when the dog returned.','皱眉转身不是微笑。','meaning'),[q('What did the dog do when it returned?','wagged its tail','hid under the train seat','smelled of smoke','小狗摇着尾巴回到门口。',1,'context'),q('How was the nurse’s smile described?','tired but genuine','angry and forced','invisible and absent','护士露出了疲惫但真诚的笑容。',1,'context'),q('What does smile mean as a verb?','make the corners of the mouth turn up','hit something with a flat hand','spread gel over a surface','smile 作动词指嘴角上扬。',1,'meaning'),q('What is a smile in the nurse example?','a facial expression with upturned mouth corners','a type of furnace','a sudden sharp pain','护士例句中的 smile 指笑容。',1,'meaning')]);
P('smirch','Smirch is from Middle English smirchen, “to stain”; it means make dirty or damage a reputation with disgrace.',C('smirch.s1','玷污；污损名誉','The forged report threatened to smirch the scientist’s reputation, although the investigation later cleared her.','伪造的报告险些玷污这位科学家的名誉，不过调查后来证明她清白。','The forged report threatened to smirch her reputation / although the investigation / later cleared her.','smirch.s1 指弄脏表面，也可比喻使名誉蒙羞。','伪造报告试图损害名誉。'),M('The forged report smirched her reputation by publicly proving every allegation true and clearing her name.','The false report tried to stain her reputation, but the inquiry cleared her.','调查证明清白，不是证实指控。','meaning'),[q('What threatened to smirch the scientist’s reputation?','a forged report','a verified award','a clean laboratory window','伪造的报告威胁到科学家的名誉。',1,'context'),q('What did the investigation eventually do?','cleared her','confirmed the false report','closed the laboratory','调查后来证明她清白。',1,'context'),q('What does smirch mean figuratively?','damage a person’s good name','improve a room’s appearance','smell a hidden fire','smirch 比喻损害某人的名誉。',1,'meaning'),q('What could smirch a previously spotless page?','a dark stain rubbed across it','a blank clean sheet placed beside it','a smile from the reader','把深色污迹抹到干净页面上会玷污它。',1,'context')]);
P('smirk','Smirk may be related to an older word for smiling; it can be a self-satisfied smile, often at another’s trouble, or smile in that way.',[C('smirk.s1','得意的笑；幸灾乐祸的笑','When the rival team missed the final shot, one spectator smirked instead of offering sympathy.','对手队投丢最后一球时，一名观众没有表示同情，反而露出幸灾乐祸的笑。','One spectator smirked / when the rival team missed / the final shot.','smirk.s1 作名词，指自鸣得意或因别人倒霉而暗自高兴的笑。','观众看到对手失误而幸灾乐祸。'),C('smirk.s2','得意地笑；假笑','The student smirked as if he already knew the answer, but the teacher asked him to explain his reasoning.','学生得意地笑着，仿佛已经知道答案，但老师让他解释推理过程。','The student smirked / as if he knew the answer / and was asked to explain.','smirk.s2 作动词，指露出自满、往往不友好的笑。','学生的笑显得自以为是。')],M('The spectator smirked sympathetically after the rivals won and congratulated them warmly.','The spectator gave a self-satisfied, unkind smile when the rival team missed.','真诚同情并祝贺胜者不符合幸灾乐祸的 smirk。','meaning'),[q('What happened before the spectator smirked?','the rival team missed its final shot','the spectator’s team won a trophy','the teacher assigned homework','对手队投丢最后一球后，观众露出得意的笑。',1,'context'),q('What did the teacher ask the smirking student to do?','explain his reasoning','leave the classroom immediately','repair the rival team’s ball','老师让得意发笑的学生解释推理过程。',1,'context'),q('What does smirk suggest in the spectator example?','self-satisfaction at another team’s failure','warm sympathy for a winner','fear of a loud sound','这里的 smirk 暗示观众因对方失误而暗自高兴。',1,'meaning'),q('Which expression is a smirk?','a smug smile at someone else’s misfortune','a broad friendly grin of welcome','a painful grimace from a cut','看到别人倒霉而露出的自满笑容是 smirk。',1,'context')]);
P('smite','Smite comes from Old English smītan; it means hit with great force or afflict suddenly as if by a blow.',C('smite.s1','重击；突然侵袭','In the legend, a lightning bolt smote the tower during the storm and split its upper stonework.','传说中，暴风雨时一道闪电击中塔楼，劈裂了上部石构件。','A lightning bolt smote the tower / during the storm / and split its upper stonework.','smite.s1 常用于文学或正式语境，指猛击或像一击般突然侵袭。','闪电猛击塔楼并造成裂缝。'),M('The lightning smote the tower gently without touching it or causing any change.','The lightning struck the tower forcefully and split its stonework.','未接触且毫无影响不符合 smite 的猛烈打击义。','meaning'),[q('What smote the tower?','a lightning bolt','a soft cloth','a small paper label','一道闪电击中了塔楼。',1,'context'),q('What damage followed?','the upper stonework split','the tower became a smartphone','the stonework turned into snow','塔楼上部石构件被劈裂。',1,'context'),q('What does smite mean?','strike with great force or afflict suddenly','improve a room’s appearance','move slowly without energy','smite 指猛烈击打或突然侵袭。',1,'meaning'),q('Which event could be described as smiting a tree?','a powerful lightning strike splitting its trunk','a leaf falling gently beside it','a gardener smiling at it','强烈闪电劈裂树干可称为 smiting a tree。',1,'context')]);
P('smog','Smog blends smoke and fog; it means air pollution that looks like a mixture of smoke and fog.',C('smog.s1','烟雾；雾霾','A brown layer of smog hung over the city until the wind cleared the air in the afternoon.','一层棕色烟雾笼罩着城市，直到下午风把空气吹散。','A brown layer of smog hung over the city / until the wind / cleared the air.','smog.s1 指看起来像烟和雾混合物的空气污染。','棕色污染层在风起后消散。'),M('A layer of smog hung over the city even though the air was perfectly clean and contained no pollution.','Polluted air resembling a mixture of smoke and fog covered the city.','洁净无污染的空气不构成 smog。','meaning'),[q('What color was the smog layer?','brown','bright blue','transparent green','笼罩城市的烟雾呈棕色。',1,'context'),q('What cleared the air in the afternoon?','the wind','a snowfall inside the station','a new phone application','下午风把空气吹散。',1,'context'),q('What is smog?','air pollution resembling smoke mixed with fog','a clean cloud of water vapor','a wet mixture used in construction','smog 指像烟雾混合物的空气污染。',1,'meaning'),q('Which condition is smog?','polluted air forming a hazy layer over a city','a clear day with no pollution','smoke trapped inside a sealed furnace only','污染空气形成城市上空的雾霾层，就是 smog。',1,'context')]);
P('smoke','Smoke comes from Old English smoca; it can mean the gas from burning, breathe tobacco smoke, or produce smoke.',[C('smoke.s1','烟；烟雾','Smoke drifted from the wood stove and curled toward the open window.','烟从柴炉里飘出，盘旋着飘向敞开的窗户。','Smoke drifted from the wood stove / and curled / toward the open window.','smoke.s1 作名词，指物质燃烧时产生的灰色或黑色气体。','柴炉燃烧产生烟。'),C('smoke.s2','吸烟','The doctor advised Sam not to smoke because cigarettes were worsening his breathing.','医生建议萨姆不要吸烟，因为香烟使他的呼吸状况恶化。','The doctor advised Sam not to smoke / because cigarettes / worsened his breathing.','smoke.s2 作动词，指吸入香烟等产生的烟。','医生建议病人戒烟以改善呼吸。'),C('smoke.s3','冒烟','The old engine began to smoke after its oil line leaked onto the hot exhaust.','机油管漏出的油滴到高温排气管上后，旧发动机开始冒烟。','The old engine began to smoke / after oil leaked / onto the hot exhaust.','smoke.s3 作动词，指产生烟雾。','漏油遇到高温部件后发动机冒烟。')],M('The stove produced smoke while burning wood even though it released no gas or visible particles.','Burning wood produced a visible gray gas that drifted from the stove.','烟就是燃烧时产生的可见气体。','meaning'),[q('Where did the smoke drift from?','the wood stove','the open window outside','the doctor’s office','烟从柴炉里飘出。',1,'context'),q('Why did the doctor advise Sam not to smoke?','cigarettes were worsening his breathing','the stove needed more wood','his engine oil had cooled','香烟使萨姆的呼吸状况恶化。',1,'context'),q('What caused the old engine to smoke?','oil leaked onto the hot exhaust','the window was open','the doctor gave advice','机油漏到高温排气管上后，发动机开始冒烟。',3,'context'),q('What does smoke mean as a noun?','gas produced when something burns','a thin layer of gel','a sharp sound of impact','smoke 作名词指燃烧产生的烟雾。',1,'meaning')]);
P('smoker','Smoker is formed from smoke and -er; it means a person who regularly smokes cigarettes, cigars, or a pipe.',C('smoker.s1','吸烟者','The clinic offered a support group for each smoker who wanted help quitting cigarettes.','诊所为每位想戒烟的吸烟者提供互助小组。','The clinic offered a support group / for each smoker / who wanted to quit cigarettes.','smoker.s1 指有吸烟习惯的人。','诊所为想戒烟的人提供帮助。'),M('The clinic called Ana a smoker although she had never used tobacco in any form.','The clinic called a regular tobacco user a smoker.','从未吸烟的人不符合 smoker 的含义。','meaning'),[q('Who could join the clinic’s group?','a smoker who wanted to quit','someone who had never used tobacco','a mechanic repairing a furnace','诊所为想戒烟的吸烟者提供互助小组。',1,'context'),q('What did the clinic offer?','help with quitting cigarettes','free cigarettes for patients','a small farm lease','诊所提供戒烟支持。',1,'context'),q('What is a smoker?','someone who regularly uses tobacco','someone who smells a campfire once','a machine that burns ore','smoker 指有吸烟习惯的人。',1,'meaning'),q('Which person is a smoker?','a person who regularly smokes a pipe','a person who never tried tobacco','a person near a campfire once','经常抽烟斗的人是 smoker。',1,'context')]);
P('smoking','Smoking is the -ing form of smoke; as a noun it means the habit or act of inhaling tobacco smoke.',C('smoking.s1','吸烟','The apartment building banned smoking in shared corridors because smoke drifted into neighboring homes.','公寓楼禁止在共用走廊吸烟，因为烟会飘进邻居家中。','The building banned smoking in shared corridors / because smoke drifted / into neighboring homes.','smoking.s1 作名词，指吸入烟草烟雾的行为或习惯。','走廊吸烟使烟雾飘进住户家中。'),M('The building banned smoking although no one inhaled tobacco or produced smoke there.','The rule banned inhaling tobacco smoke in shared corridors.','禁令针对的是吸烟行为。','meaning'),[q('Where did the building ban smoking?','in shared corridors','inside the clinic group only','on the garden path','大楼禁止在共用走廊吸烟。',1,'context'),q('Why was it banned there?','smoke drifted into neighboring homes','the corridors were used for farming','the building wanted more smoke','烟雾会飘进邻居家中，所以禁止走廊吸烟。',1,'context'),q('What does smoking mean here?','the act of inhaling tobacco smoke','gas from a wood stove','a sharp impact sound','smoking 指吸入烟草烟雾的行为。',1,'meaning'),q('Which rule addresses smoking?','a ban on tobacco use in shared indoor areas','a rule about opening windows','a ban on carrying phones','禁止在共用室内区域吸烟属于 smoking 禁令。',1,'context')]);
P('smoky','Smoky is formed from smoke and -y; it means filled with smoke or having the taste and odor of smoke.',C('smoky.s1','多烟的；有烟熏味的','The kitchen grew smoky when the onions charred, so Mira switched on the extractor fan.','洋葱烧焦后厨房里烟雾弥漫，米拉便打开了抽油烟机。','The kitchen grew smoky / when the onions charred / so Mira turned on the fan.','smoky.s1 指充满烟雾，或带有烟的气味、味道。','烧焦食物使厨房充满烟。'),M('The kitchen was smoky although nothing burned and the air had no odor or smoke.','The charred onions filled the kitchen with smoke.','没有燃烧或烟味的环境不是 smoky。','meaning'),[q('What made the kitchen smoky?','the onions charred','the fan stopped all cooking','a cold engine started outside','洋葱烧焦使厨房烟雾弥漫。',1,'context'),q('What did Mira switch on?','the extractor fan','a smartphone camera','a smelting furnace','米拉打开了抽油烟机。',1,'context'),q('What does smoky mean?','filled with smoke or tasting of smoke','completely odorless','small in scale','smoky 指充满烟雾或带烟熏味。',1,'meaning'),q('Which room is smoky?','one where burnt food fills the air with smoke','a clean room with fresh air','a room with no fire or odor','空气中充满烧焦烟雾的房间是 smoky。',1,'context')]);
P('smooth','Smooth comes from Old English smōth; it can mean even, without problems or insincerely over-polite, or make a surface flat/remove difficulties.',[C('smooth.s1','光滑的；平整的','The carpenter sanded the rough edge until the tabletop felt smooth under her palm.','木匠把粗糙边缘打磨到桌面摸起来平滑为止。','The carpenter sanded the edge / until the tabletop felt smooth / under her palm.','smooth.s1 指表面平坦、没有凸块或凹坑。','打磨让桌面变得平整。'),C('smooth.s2','平稳的；顺利的；圆滑的','The transfer went smoothly, but the smooth salesman’s promises sounded too polished to be sincere.','交接过程很顺利，不过那位圆滑销售员的承诺过于漂亮，听起来并不真诚。','The transfer went smoothly / but the salesman’s polished promises / sounded insincere.','smooth.s2 可指进展顺利，也可形容过分圆滑而不真诚的言行。','同一句呈现顺利过程与圆滑承诺。'),C('smooth.s3','使光滑；缓和','The mediator helped smooth tensions between the neighbors before the dispute reached court.','调解员在纠纷诉诸法院前，帮助缓和了邻居之间的紧张关系。','The mediator helped smooth tensions / between the neighbors / before court.','smooth.s3 作动词，指把表面弄平或消除问题、缓和关系。','调解员使紧张关系缓和。')],M('The carpenter made the tabletop smooth by leaving every splinter and deep groove untouched.','The carpenter sanded away rough spots until the surface felt even.','保留毛刺和深沟不会使表面 smooth。','meaning'),[q('What did the carpenter do?','sanded the tabletop’s rough edge','covered it with slush','smoked it in a stove','木匠打磨了桌面的粗糙边缘。',1,'context'),q('What did the mediator try to smooth?','tensions between neighbors','the salesman’s jacket','grooves in the table','调解员试图缓和邻居间的紧张关系。',3,'context'),q('What does smooth mean about the tabletop?','even and without rough spots','full of deep grooves','a person who smokes','smooth 描述桌面时指平滑。',1,'meaning'),q('What does smooth mean as a verb in “smooth tensions”?','reduce or remove difficulties','make a surface rougher','produce smoke','smooth tensions 指缓和、消除紧张关系。',3,'meaning')]);
P('smoothly','Smoothly is formed from smooth and -ly; it means without difficulty or interruption, or with even movement/speech.',[C('smoothly.s1','顺利地；平稳地','The software update installed smoothly overnight, and every file was ready the next morning.','软件更新在夜间顺利安装，第二天早上所有文件都已就绪。','The software update installed smoothly / overnight / and every file was ready.','smoothly.s1 指过程没有困难、中断或突然变化。','更新顺利完成且文件可用。'),C('smoothly.s2','平滑地；流畅地','The skater moved smoothly across the ice, linking each turn without a pause.','滑冰者在冰面上流畅地移动，每个转弯都衔接自然，没有停顿。','The skater moved smoothly across the ice / linking each turn / without a pause.','smoothly.s2 指动作流畅均匀，也可形容说话流利。','动作均匀且没有停顿。')],M('The update installed smoothly, stopping every few seconds and leaving files unusable.','The update completed without interruption, leaving files ready.','不断中断且文件不可用不是 smoothly。','meaning'),[q('When did the update install?','overnight','during the skater’s performance','before the software existed','软件更新在夜间安装完成。',1,'context'),q('How did the skater link the turns?','without a pause','with a stop after each turn','by walking off the ice','滑冰者的转弯衔接自然，没有停顿。',2,'context'),q('What does smoothly mean about the update?','without difficulty or interruption','with a rough surface','in a secretive way','smoothly 描述更新时指顺利且不中断。',1,'meaning'),q('What does smoothly mean about the skater?','evenly and fluently','with repeated abrupt stops','with a strong smoke odor','smoothly 描述滑冰动作时指平稳流畅。',2,'meaning')]);
P('smoothness','Smoothness is formed from smooth and -ness; it means an even surface or an easy, uninterrupted manner.',C('smoothness.s1','平滑；流畅','The smoothness of the polished lens allowed light to pass without distortion.','镜片表面的平滑让光线通过时没有发生畸变。','The smoothness of the polished lens / allowed light to pass / without distortion.','smoothness.s1 可指表面均匀，也可指过程或表达流畅无阻。','镜面光滑有助于光线通过。'),M('The lens’s smoothness distorted the light because its surface was covered in deep scratches.','The lens’s even surface let light pass without distortion.','布满深划痕的表面不平滑。','meaning'),[q('What did the lens’s smoothness allow?','light to pass without distortion','smoke to remain trapped','the lens to become a phone','镜片平滑使光线通过时没有畸变。',1,'context'),q('What was polished?','the lens','the stove','the garden path','被抛光的是镜片。',1,'context'),q('What does smoothness mean about a surface?','an even, unrough condition','a sudden sharp impact','a contagious disease','smoothness 描述表面时指平滑状态。',1,'meaning'),q('What else can smoothness describe?','an easy, uninterrupted way of speaking or working','a dirty appearance','a period of falling sales','smoothness 也可指表达或过程流畅无阻。',1,'meaning')]);
P('smother','Smother comes from Middle English smortheren; it can mean make breathing difficult, cover food thickly, or suppress a feeling.',[C('smother.s1','使窒息；闷住','The rescue team opened the sealed room because smoke threatened to smother anyone trapped inside.','救援队打开密闭房间，因为烟雾可能使困在里面的人窒息。','Smoke threatened to smother anyone / trapped inside / the sealed room.','smother.s1 指用覆盖物或烟雾使人难以呼吸。','密闭房间的烟雾造成窒息危险。'),C('smother.s2','厚厚覆盖（食物）','At the diner, guests could smother their baked potatoes with sour cream and chopped chives.','在餐馆，客人可以在烤土豆上厚厚地加酸奶油和切碎的细香葱。','Guests could smother their potatoes / with sour cream / and chopped chives.','smother.s2 指用酱汁、奶油等把食物完全覆盖。','酸奶油和香葱覆盖烤土豆。'),C('smother.s3','抑制；压下情绪','She tried to smother her laughter during the solemn speech, pressing her lips together.','庄严演讲期间，她抿紧嘴唇，努力忍住笑声。','She tried to smother her laughter / during the solemn speech / pressing her lips together.','smother.s3 指隐藏强烈情绪，或阻止某事发展。','她努力压下笑意。')],M('The smoke smothered no one because everyone inside breathed freely through clean air.','The smoke made breathing difficult for anyone trapped in the sealed room.','烟雾导致呼吸困难，正是 smother 的含义。','meaning'),[q('What threatened to smother people in the room?','smoke','sour cream','the speech','密闭房间里的烟雾可能使人窒息。',1,'context'),q('What could diners add to baked potatoes?','sour cream and chopped chives','industrial sludge','a phone case','客人可在烤土豆上加酸奶油和细香葱。',2,'context'),q('What did she try to smother?','her laughter','the rescue team','the potato','她在演讲期间努力忍住笑声。',3,'context'),q('What does smother mean in the emotional example?','hide or suppress a feeling','cover food with sauce','produce a cloud of smoke','此处 smother 指压下、不表现某种情绪。',3,'meaning')]);
P('smoulder','Smoulder is from Middle English smolderen; it can mean burn slowly with smoke but no flame, or persist as a strong unexpressed feeling.',[C('smoulder.s1','闷烧；无焰燃烧','The campfire continued to smoulder beneath the ash after its visible flames had gone out.','明火熄灭后，篝火仍在灰烬下闷烧。','The campfire continued to smoulder / beneath the ash / after flames went out.','smoulder.s1 指物质缓慢燃烧、冒烟但没有火焰。','灰烬下仍在闷烧。'),C('smoulder.s2','（情绪）郁积','Resentment smouldered between the partners for months because neither discussed the unpaid debt.','由于双方都不谈未偿债务，两位合伙人之间的怨恨持续郁积了数月。','Resentment smouldered between the partners / for months / over the unpaid debt.','smoulder.s2 比喻强烈情绪长时间存在却未表达。','未解决的债务使怨恨暗中持续。')],M('The campfire smouldered by burning brightly with tall, visible flames.','It burned slowly and smoked beneath the ash without flames.','有高大明火不是 smoulder 的无焰闷烧状态。','meaning'),[q('Where did the fire smoulder?','beneath the ash','inside a clinic corridor','under a layer of cream','篝火在灰烬下继续闷烧。',1,'context'),q('How long did the resentment smoulder?','for months','for one second','until the partners resolved the debt immediately','怨恨持续郁积了数月。',2,'context'),q('What does smoulder mean about a fire?','burn slowly with smoke but no flame','shine with tall flames','freeze into wet snow','smoulder 描述火时指冒烟但没有明火地缓慢燃烧。',1,'meaning'),q('What can smoulder figuratively?','resentment that persists without being expressed','a polished lens','a small farm crop','未表达却持续存在的怨恨可以 smoulder。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sms','SMS abbreviates short message service; it commonly means a short text message sent from one mobile phone to another.',C('sms.s1','短信；手机短信','The clinic sent an SMS reminding each patient to bring the appointment card on Monday.','诊所发短信提醒每位病人周一带上预约卡。','The clinic sent an SMS / reminding each patient / to bring the appointment card.','sms.s1 指通过手机短信服务发送的简短文字消息。','诊所用短信发送提醒。'),M('The clinic sent an SMS by mailing a paper letter that took weeks to arrive.','The clinic sent a short message directly to the patient’s mobile phone.','数周后寄达的纸信不是 SMS。','meaning'),[q('What did the clinic send?','a reminder message','a metal slug','a paper letter by post','诊所发了一条提醒短信。',1,'context'),q('What were patients reminded to bring?','the appointment card','a garden hose','a train suitcase','短信提醒病人带预约卡。',1,'context'),q('What does SMS stand for?','short message service','smooth movement system','small metal smelting','SMS 是 short message service 的缩写。',1,'meaning'),q('What is an SMS in ordinary use?','a short text sent from one mobile phone to another','a long printed report delivered by courier','a voice call with no text','SMS 通常指手机之间发送的简短文字。',1,'meaning')]);
P('smudge','Smudge is from an older verb meaning to soil; it can mean a blurred dirty mark or spread ink, paint, or makeup until unclear.',C('smudge.s1','污迹；弄模糊','A blue ink smudge blurred the date on the form after the wet page brushed against the clerk’s sleeve.','湿纸页蹭到职员袖子后，蓝墨污迹把表格上的日期弄模糊了。','A blue ink smudge blurred the date / after the wet page / brushed the sleeve.','smudge.s1 可指模糊污迹，也可指把墨水、颜料或化妆品抹花。','湿墨被蹭开，日期看不清了。'),M('The wet form had no smudge because its blue ink remained sharp and untouched.','The ink blurred into a dirty mark when the wet page rubbed against a sleeve.','墨迹没有被蹭开就不会形成 smudge。','meaning'),[q('What did the ink smudge blur?','the date on the form','the phone screen','the train window','蓝墨污迹把表格上的日期弄模糊了。',1,'context'),q('What caused the mark to spread?','the wet page brushed against a sleeve','the ink had dried for a week','the form was in a clean folder','湿纸页蹭到袖子上，墨迹便被抹开。',1,'context'),q('What is a smudge?','a blurred dirty mark','a short text message','a slow-moving garden animal','smudge 指模糊的污迹。',1,'meaning'),q('What does it mean to smudge makeup?','rub it so it becomes blurred','apply it evenly without touching it','send it by text message','smudge 化妆品指把妆抹花。',1,'meaning')]);
P('smug','Smug was recorded for neat or trim appearance; it now often means self-satisfied or showing calm satisfaction.',[C('smug.s1','自鸣得意的；自满的','After boasting that he alone understood the puzzle, the smug contestant ignored the teammates who had helped him.','夸口说只有自己懂这道题后，这名自鸣得意的选手无视了帮助过他的队友。','The smug contestant boasted / that only he understood / and ignored his teammates.','smug.s1 指对自己过分满意，仿佛觉得胜过别人。','他夸大自己的功劳并无视队友。'),C('smug.s2','（表情）自得而安然的','With her work finished and the deadline met, Priya wore a smug smile and leaned back calmly.','工作完成且赶上截止期限后，普里娅露出自得的笑容，平静地靠了回去。','Priya wore a smug smile / after finishing the work / and meeting the deadline.','smug.s2 描述表情时指闭口、略抬下巴的自得神情。','她完成工作后神情满足。')],M('The smug contestant admitted that every teammate had solved the puzzle while he contributed nothing.','The contestant acted as if his own ability made him superior to the team.','承认自己毫无贡献、没有自满表现与 smug 相反。','meaning'),[q('What did the contestant boast?','that only he understood the puzzle','that he could not read','that teammates had no role','选手夸口说只有自己懂这道题。',1,'context'),q('How did Priya look after finishing on time?','calmly satisfied','angry and confused','sleepy and unable to stand','普里娅完成工作后神情自得而平静。',2,'context'),q('What does smug mean about the contestant?','too pleased with himself and superior toward others','quietly asleep','dirty and careless','smug 描述选手时指自鸣得意、自认为高人一等。',1,'meaning'),q('What does a smug smile show?','calm self-satisfaction','fear of a sharp sound','a wet dirty stain','smug smile 表现出自得而满足的神情。',2,'meaning')]);
P('smuggle','Smuggle is probably from Low German smuggelen, “to creep”; it can mean illegally transport goods across a border or secretly take an item into a forbidden place.',[C('smuggle.s1','走私','Customs officers stopped a van carrying untaxed tobacco that smugglers planned to take across the border.','海关人员拦下了一辆装有未纳税烟草的货车，走私者原计划把货物运过边境。','Officers stopped a van carrying untaxed tobacco / planned to cross / the border.','smuggle.s1 指违法把货物运入或运出一个国家。','未纳税烟草被准备偷运过境。'),C('smuggle.s2','偷偷带入；夹带','The student tried to smuggle a phone into the exam hall, where electronic devices were forbidden.','学生试图把手机偷偷带进禁止使用电子设备的考场。','The student tried to smuggle a phone / into the exam hall / where devices were forbidden.','smuggle.s2 指偷偷把不允许的物品带进某处。','手机被禁止带入考场。')],M('The officers called it smuggling although the tobacco was declared, taxed, and legally transported.','The tobacco was being carried illegally across the border without required tax.','申报、纳税且合法运输不属于走私。','meaning'),[q('What did the van carry?','untaxed tobacco','a smartphone for an exam','fresh vegetables from a village','货车装有未纳税烟草。',1,'context'),q('Where did the student take the phone?','into the exam hall','across a mountain field','into a smelting furnace','学生试图把手机偷偷带进考场。',2,'context'),q('What does smuggle mean in the customs example?','transport goods illegally across a border','pay tax on a legal shipment','send a short message','海关例句中的 smuggle 指违法走私货物。',1,'meaning'),q('What does smuggle mean in the exam example?','secretly take a forbidden item into a place','leave a phone at the doorway','repair a device before a test','考场例句中的 smuggle 指偷偷带入禁带物品。',2,'meaning')]);
P('smuggling','Smuggling is formed from smuggle and -ing; it means the illegal movement of goods across a border without paying required tax.',C('smuggling.s1','走私（行为）','The report linked the seizure to smuggling because the imported cigarettes crossed the border without the required tax.','报告把这次查获与走私联系起来，因为进口香烟过境时没有缴纳应付税款。','The report linked the seizure to smuggling / because cigarettes crossed the border / without tax.','smuggling.s1 指未经纳税或许可而违法地把货物运入或运出国家。','未缴税的香烟被非法运过边境。'),M('The report described the shipment as smuggling although it was declared, licensed, and taxed.','The shipment was smuggling because the goods crossed without required tax.','申报、获批并缴税的货物不构成走私。','meaning'),[q('What goods had crossed the border?','imported cigarettes','fresh garden compost','an appointment card','过境货物是进口香烟。',1,'context'),q('Why did the report link the seizure to smuggling?','the required tax had not been paid','the cigarettes were grown on two acres','a message arrived by phone','香烟过境时没有缴纳应付税款。',1,'context'),q('What is smuggling?','illegal movement of goods across a border','legal import with all duties paid','a short mobile text','smuggling 指货物跨境走私。',1,'meaning'),q('Which shipment involves smuggling?','goods cross a border without required tax','licensed cargo is declared and taxed','a domestic parcel is delivered legally','未申报且未缴税的跨境货物涉及 smuggling。',1,'context')]);
P('snack','Snack is probably related to Dutch snacken, “to bite”; it can mean a small meal between meals or eat a little between meals.',[C('snack.s1','小吃；零食','Before the evening class, Jamal ate a small snack of yogurt and fruit instead of a full dinner.','晚间课程前，贾迈勒吃了酸奶和水果这份小点心，而不是一顿正餐。','Jamal ate a small snack / of yogurt and fruit / before class.','snack.s1 作名词，指两餐之间吃的一小份食物。','酸奶和水果作为正餐之间的小吃。'),C('snack.s2','吃零食','The hikers stopped to snack on nuts while they rested beside the trail.','徒步者在小径旁休息时停下来吃坚果。','The hikers stopped to snack on nuts / while resting / beside the trail.','snack.s2 作动词，指两餐之间吃少量食物。','徒步者休息时吃一点坚果。')],M('Jamal ate a snack that was a large three-course dinner served as his main meal.','Jamal ate a small portion of yogurt and fruit between meals.','大份正餐并非通常意义上的 snack。','meaning'),[q('What was Jamal’s snack made of?','yogurt and fruit','three courses of hot food','a phone and a label','贾迈勒的小吃是酸奶和水果。',1,'context'),q('What did the hikers snack on?','nuts','smoked metal','wet snow','徒步者休息时吃坚果。',2,'context'),q('What does snack mean as a noun?','a small amount of food between meals','a full feast','a type of border tax','snack 作名词指两餐之间的小吃。',1,'meaning'),q('What does snack mean as a verb?','eat a little food between meals','smell something from afar','carry goods illegally','snack 作动词指吃些零食。',1,'meaning')]);
P('snacks','Snacks is the plural of snack; it refers to small foods such as crisps, nuts, or biscuits eaten between meals.',C('snacks.s1','小吃；点心（复数）','The meeting organizer set out snacks—nuts, crackers, and apple slices—so guests could eat between sessions.','会议组织者摆出坚果、薄脆饼和苹果片等点心，让来宾能在各场会议之间吃一些。','The organizer set out snacks / so guests could eat / between sessions.','snacks.s1 是 snack 的复数，指两餐之间吃的小份食品。','桌上摆着多种点心供来宾取用。'),M('The organizer called the snacks a single full dinner served to every guest.','The organizer provided small foods to eat between meeting sessions.','少量间食不是一顿完整晚餐。','meaning'),[q('What kinds of snacks were offered?','nuts, crackers, and apple slices','a three-course hot dinner','industrial ore and stone','会议上提供了坚果、薄脆饼和苹果片。',1,'context'),q('When could guests eat them?','between sessions','only after leaving the building','during the previous month','来宾可以在会议各场次之间吃点心。',1,'context'),q('What does snacks refer to?','small foods eaten between meals','one full formal dinner','a short message by phone','snacks 指两餐之间吃的小份食品。',1,'meaning'),q('Which table has snacks?','one with nuts, crackers, and fruit for a break','one with only a large plated dinner','one with repair tools','摆着坚果、薄脆饼和水果供休息时食用的桌子上有 snacks。',1,'context')]);
P('snag','Snag is of uncertain origin; it can mean an unexpected difficulty, or catch fabric on a sharp point/get something with a quick effort.',[C('snag.s1','意外障碍；小麻烦','The only snag in the launch plan was a missing permit, which delayed the opening by one day.','开业计划中唯一的麻烦是缺少许可证，导致开门推迟了一天。','The only snag was a missing permit / which delayed the opening / by one day.','snag.s1 指计划中意外出现的小困难或障碍。','缺许可证造成一天延误。'),C('snag.s2','钩住；抢到','Maya snagged her sleeve on a nail while carrying boxes and had to mend the torn fabric.','玛雅搬箱子时袖子被钉子钩住，只好缝补撕破的布料。','Maya snagged her sleeve on a nail / while carrying boxes / and mended it.','snag.s2 作动词可指衣物被尖物钩住，也可指迅速获得某物。','袖子被钉子钩破。')],M('The plan had a snag although everything was approved early and no delay or problem occurred.','A missing permit created an unexpected difficulty and delayed the opening.','没有问题、没有延误不能算 snag。','meaning'),[q('What caused the plan’s snag?','a missing permit','too many extra permits','a fast software update','开业计划的麻烦是缺少许可证。',1,'context'),q('What caught Maya’s sleeve?','a nail','a piece of fruit','a text message','钉子钩住了玛雅的袖子。',2,'context'),q('What does snag mean as a noun?','an unexpected difficulty','a small piece of food','a self-satisfied smile','snag 作名词指意外的小麻烦。',1,'meaning'),q('What does snag mean as a verb in the sleeve example?','catch fabric on a sharp point','smooth a rough surface','send goods across a border','袖子例句中的 snag 指衣物被尖物钩住。',1,'meaning')]);
P('snail','Snail comes from Old English snægl; it is a small animal with a soft body, a round shell, and slow movement.',C('snail.s1','蜗牛','A snail withdrew into its round shell when the gardener’s watering can rattled nearby.','园丁的洒水壶在旁边发出响声时，一只蜗牛缩回了圆壳里。','A snail withdrew into its round shell / when the watering can / rattled nearby.','snail.s1 指身体柔软、有圆形外壳并缓慢移动的小动物。','受到惊扰后蜗牛缩进壳中。'),M('The snail withdrew into a shell although it had no shell and was a fast-running mammal.','The soft-bodied snail protected itself by withdrawing into its shell.','有壳蜗牛的特征与无壳、快速的哺乳动物相反。','meaning'),[q('What did the snail withdraw into?','its round shell','a smartphone case','a furnace','蜗牛缩回了圆壳里。',1,'context'),q('What made the watering can noticeable?','it rattled nearby','it smelled of lime','it smoothed the path','洒水壶在附近发出响声。',1,'context'),q('What is a snail?','a slow-moving animal with a soft body and shell','a shell-less slug','a metal bullet','snail 指身体柔软、有壳且行动缓慢的动物。',1,'meaning'),q('Which creature is a snail?','a soft-bodied animal that carries a round shell','a fast animal with no legs or shell','a phone with apps','带着圆壳爬行的软体动物是 snail。',1,'context')]);
P('snake','Snake comes from Old English snaca; it can mean a long legless animal or move/extend in long winding curves.',[C('snake.s1','蛇','The snake slid beneath a fallen log, leaving the hikers to watch from a safe distance.','蛇滑进倒木下，徒步者留在安全距离外观察。','The snake slid beneath a fallen log / while hikers watched / from a safe distance.','snake.s1 指没有腿、沿地面滑行的细长动物。','蛇从倒木下滑过。'),C('snake.s2','蜿蜒伸展；蛇行','A narrow road snakes up the hillside, curving around trees toward the lookout.','一条窄路蜿蜒上山，绕过树木通向观景台。','A narrow road snakes up the hillside / curving around trees / toward the lookout.','snake.s2 作动词，指沿弯曲路线蜿蜒移动或延伸。','道路沿山坡弯曲向上。')],M('The snake slid beneath the log on four legs and walked upright past the hikers.','The legless snake moved by sliding beneath the fallen log.','蛇没有腿，不能四足行走。','meaning'),[q('Where did the snake slide?','beneath a fallen log','up a road to the lookout','into a phone app','蛇滑进了倒木下。',1,'context'),q('What did the road do on the hillside?','curved around trees toward the lookout','ran straight across a flat room','ended at the harbor','窄路绕过树木蜿蜒通向观景台。',2,'context'),q('What is a snake as an animal?','a long legless animal that slides along the ground','a soft-bodied animal with a shell','a wet mixture of mud','snake 指沿地面滑行的细长无腿动物。',1,'meaning'),q('What does it mean for a road to snake?','extend in long curves','have a smooth even surface','stop after a brief delay','道路 snakes 指蜿蜒延伸。',2,'meaning')]);
P('snap','Snap is probably imitative of a short sharp sound; it can mean break suddenly, speak angrily/lose control, a sharp sound or informal photo, or done hastily.',[C('snap.s1','啪地折断；绷断','The dry twig snapped under one boot, making a sharp sound in the quiet woods.','干树枝在一只靴子下啪地折断，在安静的树林里发出清脆声响。','The dry twig snapped under one boot / making a sharp sound / in the woods.','snap.s1 指突然折断，通常伴有短促清脆的声音。','树枝被踩断并发出啪声。'),C('snap.s2','厉声说；突然失控','After hours of delay, the tired driver snapped at the clerk who asked for the same form again.','延误数小时后，疲惫的司机对再次索要同一张表格的职员厉声回应。','The tired driver snapped at the clerk / after hours of delay / and another request.','snap.s2 指生气地厉声说话，也可指突然失去控制。','司机因疲惫和延误而发火。'),C('snap.s3','啪的一声；快照','She took a quick snap of the harbor before the ferry departed.','渡船离开前，她快速拍了一张港口的照片。','She took a quick snap of the harbor / before the ferry / departed.','snap.s3 作名词可指短促的啪声，也可口语指快照。','她在渡船离开前拍快照。'),C('snap.s4','仓促的；突然的','The board made a snap decision without reading the full safety report.','董事会没有读完完整的安全报告就仓促作了决定。','The board made a snap decision / without reading / the full safety report.','snap.s4 作定语指仓促、未经充分考虑的。','决定作出前没有读完报告。')],M('The board made a snap decision after reading every report and discussing it for months.','The board decided hastily without considering the full safety report.','经过长时间审慎讨论后作出的决定不叫 snap decision。','meaning'),[q('What did the twig do under the boot?','broke with a sharp sound','curved up a hillside','smelled of smoke','干树枝在靴子下啪地折断。',1,'context'),q('Why did the driver snap at the clerk?','hours of delay left the driver tired','the clerk offered a useful map','the driver had slept well','长时间延误使司机疲惫，他因此发火。',1,'context'),q('What did the woman photograph before the ferry left?','the harbor','the twig','the safety report','渡船离开前，她拍了港口快照。',3,'context'),q('What does snap mean in “a snap decision”?','made quickly without careful thought','a photograph of a ship','a sudden break with a sharp sound','snap decision 指仓促、未经仔细考虑的决定。',4,'meaning')]);
P('snapshot','Snapshot combines snap and shot; it means a quick photograph or a brief account of a situation at one particular time.',[C('snapshot.s1','快照；抓拍照','The visitor took a snapshot of the old station just as the evening light reached its clock tower.','傍晚的光线刚照到钟楼时，游客拍下了老车站的快照。','The visitor took a snapshot of the old station / as evening light / reached the tower.','snapshot.s1 指用相机快速拍下的人物或场景照片。','游客快速拍下车站景色。'),C('snapshot.s2','（某时点的）概况；写照','The monthly survey offers a snapshot of household spending by recording expenses during one week.','这份月度调查通过记录一周支出，提供了家庭消费情况的阶段性概况。','The survey offers a snapshot of spending / by recording expenses / during one week.','snapshot.s2 比喻某一时点或短时间内的情况概览。','一周支出数据展示家庭消费概况。')],M('The survey was a snapshot of spending although it combined fifty years of records into a complete history.','The survey gave a brief picture of household spending during one week.','长期完整历史不属于某一短时段的 snapshot。','meaning'),[q('What did the visitor photograph?','the old station','household expenses','the ticket machine','游客拍下了老车站的快照。',1,'context'),q('How long did the survey record expenses?','one week','fifty years','one evening at the station','调查记录了一周的支出。',2,'context'),q('What does snapshot mean about the station?','a quick photograph','a long written biography','a sharp angry remark','车站例句中的 snapshot 指快照。',1,'meaning'),q('What does snapshot mean in the survey example?','a brief picture of a situation at one time','a complete history over many decades','a camera shutter sound only','调查例句中的 snapshot 指某一时段情况的简要概况。',2,'meaning')]);
})();
